{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1527695-suggested-setting-changes-to-make-crossover-easier","id":1527695,"title":"Suggested setting changes to make crossover easier","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-01-01T09:34:50-08:00","id":1527695,"title":"Suggested setting changes to make crossover easier","content":"<br /> Suggested setting changes to make crossover easier (and other crossover thoughts)<br /> <br /> <br /> It occurs to me, that of the Big Five of the Word. Wraiths, Changelings,Werewolves and Mages can be in a crossover and it's mostly ok. At least setting wise. Vampires are a sticking point, because the other 4 all have reasons to suspect them. Here's some suggested setting changes to make it easier to make the Big Five of the Word interact more easily.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Vampire and Werewolf <br /> <br /> <br /> The Gift <i>Sense Wyrm</i> now only sense things that are related to the actual Wyrm. Things that are only kinda related to it don't ping it. That means that Vampires are not automatically hated by the Garou. It's up to each Garou to decide what to do with the bloodsuckers. That means, that yes a vampire can be an ally of the pack or sept. There have been alliances before. They might still be enemies, but if a vampire is hated by the Garou it's because of the morality of their actions and not because of what they are. The spirits feel the same way.<br /> <br /> Abominations are not quite as abominable, but still discouraged.<br /> <br /> <br /> Vampire and Mage changes<br /> <br /> <br /> The enmity between vampires and mages is mostly political. The tremere betrayed the houses of Hermes. Stole their secrets, that left a huge scar.<br /> <br /> However. It has been more than 600 years since the fight happened, that's a long time. And some Tremere and Mages wonder, isn't time to let the past go? After all the Nephandus want to destroy the whole universe. Shouldn't we fight the Nephandi instead of each other? Under flag a truce was signed. Vampires and Mages are supposed to keep their mittens of each other secrets and not fight each other without provocation.<br /> <br /> The truce also meant that the underground groups of vampire and mages allies cane into the light. Groups made of members of both splats are not much common<br /> <br /> One side note. The vampires know about the other worlds, all the umbras and the dreaming. They know it all exits. After all vampires have had mystics in their ranks for at least five millenia<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Vampires and Changelings changes <br /> <br /> <br /> Changelings looooooooove the anarchs. Few things are quite as glamour filled as revolutions. And through the Anarchs, the changelings have discovered your average vampire is honestly not that Banal. The nightlife is exciting!<br /> <br /> <br /> Vampires and wraiths remain unchanged <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-01T10:28:04-08:00","id":1527696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1527695-suggested-setting-changes-to-make-crossover-easier#post1527695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Suggested setting changes to make crossover easier (and other crossover thoughts)<br /> <br /> <br /> It occurs to me, that of the Big Five of the Word. Wraiths, Changelings,Werewolves and Mages can be in a crossover and it's mostly ok. At least setting wise. Vampires are a sticking point, because the other 4 all have reasons to suspect them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Vampires don't even trust each other. And for good reason. If you want them to be better received by other things that go bump in the night, you'd have to fundamentally make them into different beings that aren't a net negative on the world.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Vampire and Werewolf<br /> <br /> <br /> The Gift <i>Sense Wyrm</i> now only sense things that are related to the actual Wyrm. </div> </div> </div>The Wyrm is a third of reality, so good luck only being &quot;kind of&quot; it. At any rate, Sense Wyrm only discerned the residue of corruption, which is so easy to have stick to you that there were multiple sidebars smacking people over the head with titles like &quot;it's not detect evil!&quot; and a rite for getting rid of it.<br /> <br /> When it came to vampires, though, that's like sweeping dirt around.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Things that are only kinda related to it don't ping it. That means that Vampires are not automatically hated by the Garou. </div> </div> </div>This is major league putting the cart before the horse. Garou and Fera don't typically bother to use any kind of Triatic sense on vampires because the vampires are unapologetically horrible people and the world would be better off without them. There wouldn't be any question of whether or not they're corrupt by nature (big yes! Hello, Eater of Souls!) because their actions are in every way supportive of it. No one is going to believe for a damned minute that they should try to be anything like a friend or even an ally of convenience with vampires.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's up to each Garou to decide what to do with the bloodsuckers. That means, that yes a vampire can be an ally of the pack or sept. There have been alliances before. They might still be enemies, but if a vampire is hated by the Garou it's because of the morality of their actions and not because of what they are. The spirits feel the same way. </div> </div> </div>This changes little to nothing. Again, because vampires are so incredibly shitty and disdain everything having to do with spiritual life (they think that Garou are &quot;just religious zealots&quot;, after all), they're pretty walking sinks for corruption, one and all. Actions have consequences. For the Garou, that's a series of blunders leading to their being in a situation like that one Atreides mission in the original Dune 2 RTS that's pretty much impossible to win without a hex editor. For vampires, it's being constantly terrible and always leaving the world worse than when they found it, at best.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Abominations are not quite as abominable, but still discouraged. </div> </div> </div>Given the above, that's not a reasonable cut back. Vampire Garou have basically just lost all their redeeming characteristics, and will slowly lose all of their Gnosis until they're utterly lost to corruption.<br /> <br /> This isn't even a torturous interpretation of Vampire itself. No one is down on Vampire like Vampire's own lore.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Vampire and Mage changes<br /> <br /> <br /> The enmity between vampires and mages is mostly political. The tremere betrayed the houses of Hermes. Stole their secrets, that left a huge scar.<br /> <br /> However. It has been more than 600 years since the fight happened, that's a long time. And some Tremere and Mages wonder, isn't time to let the past go? After all the Nephandus want to destroy the whole universe. Shouldn't we fight the Nephandi instead of each other? Under flag a truce was signed. Vampires and Mages are supposed to keep their mittens of each other secrets and not fight each other without provocation.<br /> <br /> The truce also meant that the underground groups of vampire and mages allies cane into the light. Groups made of members of both splats are not much common<br /> <br /> One side note. The vampires know about the other worlds, all the umbras and the dreaming. They know it all exits. After all vampires have had mystics in their ranks for at least five millenia </div> </div> </div>They wouldn't have access to most of it and little in the way of learning about it second hand. Auspex and Necromancy only give them access to the Shadowlands and maybe the Astral. They have nothing that gives them access to the Middle Umbra, and again, are typically so up their own asses being drains on the world that this is something that they couldn't really have. Even if you do put a vampire in the Middle Umbra, incidentally, the ambient environment tends to have unremitting sunlight that would burn them wherever they tried to hide, especially if they were big enough dunces to try going to the Aetherial Realm. The Dreaming would probably be no more hospitable, since the vampires would have to hang out in the cold, dark, nightmarish places where there's never sunlight, or else, again, probably burnt to a crisp.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Vampires and wraiths remain unchanged <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> </div> </div> </div>So, a relationship that makes the interactions of Dr. Forrester and TV's Frank look healthy and life-affirming? (^VVVVVV^)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-01T10:50:44-08:00","id":1527697,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the feedback saurs, but I just don't agree. I'm sorry.<br /> to me the evil of vampires is a product of their society,not an inherent part of their species and the wod is filled with good vampires. I totally get you disagree, I just think that vampires still have enough humanity to ally with the other spats in a crossovers","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-01T11:24:42-08:00","id":1527700,"title":"","content":"I added a little explanation to my draft doc to explain my intentions better<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/10W-TNskmv0AYFpKtOdYUMTKtwvvW23_BuURjyjdyjfc/edit?usp=drivesdk\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/10W-TNskmv0AYFpKtOdYUMTKtwvvW23_BuURjyjdyjfc/edit?usp=drivesdk\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/10W-TNskmv0AYFpKtOdYUMTKtwvvW23_BuURjyjdyjfc/edit?usp=drivesdk\" target=\"_blank\"> https://docs.google.com/document/d/10W-TNskmv0AYFpKtOdYUMTKtwvvW23_BuURjyjdyjfc/edit?usp=drivesdk </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The big changes are meant to bring forth games where vampires are just one more citizen of the night world, they're not inherently evil. Their society might be, but a vampire can be a good person just as any other splat might be.<br /> <br /> A Changeling,Wraith,Werewolf or Mage wanting his fellows to kill someone simply because he is a vampire will simply be asked<br /> <br /> \u201cOk but what has the vampire done?\u201d<br /> <br /> And if they insist the vampire must die for what he is, they'll be told to fuck off.<br /> <br /> Vampires are now judged based on the morality of their actions, not on what they are.<br /> <br /> Those changes are meant to make this easier.<br /> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-01T11:26:09-08:00","id":1527701,"title":"","content":"Posting again since my other post was glitched <br /> The big changes are meant to bring forth games where vampires are just one more citizen of the night world, they're not inherently evil. Their society might be, but a vampire can be a good person just as any other splat might be.<br /> <br /> A Changeling,Wraith,Werewolf or Mage wanting his fellows to kill someone simply because he is a vampire will simply be asked<br /> <br /> \u201cOk but what has the vampire done?\u201d<br /> <br /> And if they insist the vampire must die for wjat he is, they'll be told to fuck off.<br /> <br /> Vampires are now judged based on the morality of their actions, not on what they are.<br /> <br /> Those changes are meant to make this easier.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-01T14:18:41-08:00","id":1527706,"title":"","content":"The problem is, you're trying to change other splats, not what vampires do as a collective that will then inform the biases of the other groups.<br /> <br /> The average vampire is Humanity 4. That means the average vampire is doing lots of things of a morally dubious nature at best. Even if it might be hypocritical considering what plenty of members of the other splats get up to:<br /> <br /> V20 page 312:<br /> <br /> Humanity 5-6 - &quot;Though not constantly horrid, Kindred at this stage of Humanity are certainly at least mildly unpleasant to be around. Their laissez-faire attitudes toward others\u2019 rights offend many more moral individuals.&quot;<br /> <br /> Humanity 4 - &quot;Destruction, theft, injury \u2014 these are all tools, rather than taboos, for a vampire with Humanity 4. The vampire\u2019s own agenda becomes paramount at this point, and screw whoever gets in the way.&quot;<br /> \u200b<br /> So most vampires? They've done enough stuff that, &quot;OK but what has the vampire done?&quot; will be satisfied. The vampires that haven't crossed that line are the exception, not the rule. That's why the other splats default to hating them. Not things like Sense Wyrm.<br /> <br /> If you want changes that make vampires more functional in crossover play, you need to start with vampires themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-01T14:27:32-08:00","id":1527708,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the advice,that does give a lot of food for thought <br /> I think I know a way to make the average humanity score of. Vampires in VTM rise without changing the setting too much. Thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-01T14:30:44-08:00","id":1527709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1527695-suggested-setting-changes-to-make-crossover-easier?p=1527701#post1527701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Posting again since my other post was glitched<br /> The big changes are meant to bring forth games where vampires are just one more citizen of the night world, they're not inherently evil. Their society might be, but a vampire can be a good person just as any other splat might be.<br /> <br /> A Changeling,Wraith,Werewolf or Mage wanting his fellows to kill someone simply because he is a vampire will simply be asked<br /> <br /> \u201cOk but what has the vampire done?\u201d<br /> <br /> And if they insist the vampire must die for wjat he is, they'll be told to fuck off.<br /> <br /> Vampires are now judged based on the morality of their actions, not on what they are.<br /> <br /> Those changes are meant to make this easier.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe that the answer involves <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=c5jb9rw2eW8\" target=\"_blank\">a number of breads</a>. When you're talking about several societies of monsters that go out of their collective way not to eat people and an edge case society that consists of people who think of themselves as human (two if Imbued willing to play ball are counted), the fact that vampires have to drink blood is going to be a pretty dour opening note. The Nagaraja are flat out screwed in that case and the Giovanni don't do much better.<br /> <br /> To go back to the meta, Vampire already set up its relationship with Werewolf as heavily antagonistic before Werewolf existed. In order to mend this... you'd need to make a new game with lore that isn't heavily built in that direction. PDX probably should have done that, but the marquis value of the name was apparently a big draw.<br /> <br /> Finally, if you're saying that the vampires are evil because of their societies, does that mean that there's basically carte blanche to just end anyone who is associated with the Cam, Sabbat or whatever? And if so, how do you figure out for certain? Because they could always lie, and you can't necessarily tell that someone is a member of a sect by looking at them. Especially if they're <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shiki_(novel)\" target=\"_blank\">Sabbat infiltrators</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-01T14:40:29-08:00","id":1527710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1527695-suggested-setting-changes-to-make-crossover-easier?p=1527709#post1527709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I believe that the answer involves <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=c5jb9rw2eW8\" target=\"_blank\">a number of breads</a>. When you're talking about several societies of monsters that go out of their collective way not to eat people and an edge case society that consists of people who think of themselves as human (two if Imbued willing to play ball are counted), the fact that vampires have to drink blood is going to be a pretty dour opening note. The Nagaraja are flat out screwed in that case and the Giovanni don't do much better.<br /> <br /> To go back to the meta, Vampire already set up its relationship with Werewolf as heavily antagonistic before Werewolf existed. In order to mend this... you'd need to make a new game with lore that isn't heavily built in that direction. PDX probably should have done that, but the marquis value of the name was apparently a big draw.<br /> <br /> Finally, if you're saying that the vampires are evil because of their societies, does that mean that there's basically carte blanche to just end anyone who is associated with the Cam, Sabbat or whatever? And if so, how do you figure out for certain? Because they could always lie, and you can't necessarily tell that someone is a member of a sect by looking at them. Especially if they're <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shiki_(novel)\" target=\"_blank\">Sabbat infiltrators</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm more saying that vampiric state of being is not inherent evil but that most of them do end up doing evil stuff anyway because their whole society is wired that way.<br /> but personally, I think some small changes on how the setting works can make it sure vampire have enough of a moral backbone to not be considered &quot;kill on sight&quot; by everyone else.<br /> I personally think the fact they need to drink blood doesn't need to be that big a hurdle.,feeding is not always fatal after all. You could always find ways to feed morally. It's not easy of course,but it's doable<br /> \u200bif you are curious why I felt like doing this, the truth is is simply think a wod with certain groups with multi splat membership here and there would be cool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4621,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","user":"Nicolas Milioni","date":". 01-01-2024, 05:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-01T14:54:52-08:00","id":1527713,"title":"","content":"I think you're kinda missing the point of the JoJo reference.<br /> <br /> First, the default of VtM is that being a vampire is a curse. It has plenty of perks, but ultimately it drags them down. Low Humanity turns them into selfish sociopaths. Their societies are screwed up because they're run by older vampires, who tend to have lower Humanity because keeping up Humanity over time is in direction opposition to gaining power and control in vampire society.<br /> <br /> Second, yes, drinking blood is a problem. Let's say you have a really careful vampire that tries as hard as possible to be safe. They only accidentally kill one human per 100 vitae they consume. That's a pretty good record. That's still 3-4 dead humans a year just for the basic nightly blood cost to wake up. A character that's been a vampire for ~50 years (stated as being within starting range in most editions) has killed at least 150 people already... just from feeding accidents for basic maintenance feeding. There's going to be a point where any attempt to say that they're still a good person is going to ring morally hollow. How many accidental deaths is one vampire really worth over the potential of living for thousands of years? What moral calculus do you make that doesn't end with &quot;it's better to be rid of vampires when possible?&quot;<br /> <br /> And sure, crossover is cool and fun. There are other games out there that do monster mash games way better than the WoD does, because that's fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-01T14:59:25-08:00","id":1527715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1527695-suggested-setting-changes-to-make-crossover-easier?p=1527713#post1527713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you're kinda missing the point of the JoJo reference.<br /> <br /> First, the default of VtM is that being a vampire is a curse. It has plenty of perks, but ultimately it drags them down. Low Humanity turns them into selfish sociopaths. Their societies are screwed up because they're run by older vampires, who tend to have lower Humanity because keeping up Humanity over time is in direction opposition to gaining power and control in vampire society.<br /> <br /> Second, yes, drinking blood is a problem. Let's say you have a really careful vampire that tries as hard as possible to be safe. They only accidentally kill one human per 100 vitae they consume. That's a pretty good record. That's still 3-4 dead humans a year just for the basic nightly blood cost to wake up. A character that's been a vampire for ~50 years (stated as being within starting range in most editions) has killed at least 150 people already... just from feeding accidents for basic maintenance feeding. There's going to be a point where any attempt to say that they're still a good person is going to ring morally hollow. How many accidental deaths is one vampire really worth over the potential of living for thousands of years? What moral calculus do you make that doesn't end with &quot;it's better to be rid of vampires when possible?&quot;<br /> <br /> And sure, crossover is cool and fun. There are other games out there that do monster mash games way better than the WoD does, because that's fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>Guess I'll move on to urban shadows then. A shame <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. I really wanted to write some crossover groups but people probably wouldn't be interested","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-01T15:33:31-08:00","id":1527717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1527695-suggested-setting-changes-to-make-crossover-easier?p=1527713#post1527713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you're kinda missing the point of the JoJo reference.</div> </div> </div> </div>JoJo references tend to be a bit over the top to take fully seriously.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> First, the default of VtM is that being a vampire is a curse. It has plenty of perks, but ultimately it drags them down. Low Humanity turns them into selfish sociopaths. Their societies are screwed up because they're run by older vampires, who tend to have lower Humanity because keeping up Humanity over time is in direction opposition to gaining power and control in vampire society.<br /> <br /> Second, yes, drinking blood is a problem. Let's say you have a really careful vampire that tries as hard as possible to be safe. They only accidentally kill one human per 100 vitae they consume. That's a pretty good record. That's still 3-4 dead humans a year just for the basic nightly blood cost to wake up. A character that's been a vampire for ~50 years (stated as being within starting range in most editions) has killed at least 150 people already... just from feeding accidents for basic maintenance feeding. There's going to be a point where any attempt to say that they're still a good person is going to ring morally hollow. How many accidental deaths is one vampire really worth over the potential of living for thousands of years? What moral calculus do you make that doesn't end with &quot;it's better to be rid of vampires when possible?&quot;<br /> <br /> And sure, crossover is cool and fun. There are other games out there that do monster mash games way better than the WoD does, because that's fun. </div> </div> </div>I don't think that the problem is only with lethal casualties. Blood dolls, for example, probably give most non-vampires the jibblies, and the fact that vampires refer to humans as kine and herds probably hits a lot of side eye. And if the Black Furies and Verbena knew about Jan Pieterzoon's feeding requirement, that would be the end.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-01T16:08:13-08:00","id":1527720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1527695-suggested-setting-changes-to-make-crossover-easier?p=1527715#post1527715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Guess I'll move on to urban shadows then. A shame <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. I really wanted to write some crossover groups but people probably wouldn't be interested</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you're underestimating how antagonistic the WoD setting really is to crossover. There are long standing and deep rooted grudges and prejudices all over the place to deal with. There's the issue of wraiths being largely stuck in the Dark Kingdoms away from the mortal plane or other parts of the Umbra. Etc.<br /> <br /> People have tried, countless times, for 30 years, to make crossovers work in the WoD. You either get frustrated and give up, or just handwave a lot so the PCs get along at least.<br /> <br /> This was a huge impetus of some of the CofD changes, because the CofD was built to make it so crossover play would have less hurdles.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1527695-suggested-setting-changes-to-make-crossover-easier?p=1527717#post1527717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And if the Black Furies and Verbena knew about Jan Pieterzoon's feeding requirement, that would be the end.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe, though I struggle to think of how they would find out, without also finding out how much he's worked to keep himself on the hard path of doing the least harm possible compared to how easily he could just be a raving monster of a vampire to make his existence so much easier; esp. for the Verbena who aren't inherently feminists or egalitarians,and don't have Rage that can quickly override a more reasoned response.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-01T18:25:15-08:00","id":1527728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1527695-suggested-setting-changes-to-make-crossover-easier?p=1527720#post1527720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe, though I struggle to think of how they would find out, without also finding out how much he's worked to keep himself on the hard path of doing the least harm possible compared to how easily he could just be a raving monster of a vampire to make his existence so much easier; esp. for the Verbena who aren't inherently feminists or egalitarians,and don't have Rage that can quickly override a more reasoned response.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose I could have made the &quot;if&quot; bigger, but that would probably make the post obnoxiously <span style=\"font-size:20px\">unread</span><span style=\"font-size:22px\">able</span>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-01T18:48:13-08:00","id":1527730,"title":"","content":"My long running advice for people who want to do extended crossovers, especially with Kindred, is to use Pariah (Caitiff, Orphans, whatever we are calling Ronin now) as well as things like Risen, Created, and other oddities who are either outside the existing supernatural subcultures or are so rare as to not really have a subculture. It's actually part of the reason they exist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-01T19:14:41-08:00","id":1527731,"title":"","content":"I understand the desire to want to have more crossover between vampire characters in other games. That can be a fun thing. However, the problem is still that vampires, by their very nature, are predators of everyone else who is living. It's a scorpion and the frog situation. The burden should never be on &quot;OK, you who don't like vampires, why should this vampire not be trusted?&quot; The burden should always be &quot;OK, you who like this vampire, why should this vampire be trusted?&quot; The price for wrongly trusting a vampire is high, while the price for wrongly not distrusting a vampire tends to be very low. The economics of the situation will always prioritize not liking vampires. Regardless of the &quot;Sense Wyrm&quot; situation, this is what is always going to be the default.<br /> <br /> I am going to speak from a Werewolf perspective, as I don't really play Mage or Changeling. While I am sympathetic to wanting a more 1e &quot;crossover can be fun&quot; feel, I also want things to make sense.<br /> <br /> Let's look at the tribes most likely to have some dealings with vampires.<br /> <br /> First, the Bone Gnawers. I will say that you can justify almost any kind of relationship with Bone Gnawers. The tribe, as a whole, no longer follows the Litany in a way recognizable to the other tribes. This changed as later editions made the Bone Gnawers more upstanding Garou, but this was definitely the case in early Werewolf. The tribe has an ongoing relationship with the Nosferatu clan where they trade information. A large part of the tribe is also de facto allies with the Sabbat (!) probably because of the needs of the Central Park Caern in Sabbat held New York. Using that as an example, it would not be surprising if Bone Gnawers elsewhere had similar dealings with local vampires. Whether the Bone Gnawers actively destroy vampires or come to some sort of arrangement really depends on a lot of local factors, so the ST can justify a lot. They might always watch their back, but you can defend a lot of cooperation as an ST.<br /> <br /> Second, Glass Walkers. This tribe would be more antagonistic to vampires than the Bone Gnawers, but more prone to making deals of convenience. They don't like it, and don't trust vampires, but the environment where they work in practically requires it. Otherwise they'd be sucked into ongoing vampire wars and couldn't get anything else done. Unlike the Bone Gnawers, this is less about not giving a crap about the Litany, then about making difficult moral choices in a challenging environment for Garou where many moral dilemmas come up. Since vampires are mainly an urban environment in the setting, these first two tribes take care of almost all real encounters the typical vampire may have with a werewolf. This is going to be about rival gangs defining their turf and having their other side respect that, so only so much can happen. But it does open the possibilities for non-violent encounters.<br /> <br /> Third, Shadow Lords. Individual Lords might make any number of deals with vampires if it suits their purposes. The game even created the Bringers of Light camp in order to explain why this happens. The Shadow Lords obviously have strong enemies among the vampires, but that just creates justification for them to ally with their enemy's enemy and play vampire factions against each other. This is a case where some Shadow Lords may think &quot;this particular vampire or group of vampires can be useful to me&quot; rather than some blanket permission to intrigue with them. And other Shadow Lords might use such alliances against their tribemates. But in terms of storytelling, the ST has some options.<br /> <br /> Fourth, the Uktena and Wendigo, through their kinfolk, have some dealings with the Sabbat - which I assume are Loyalist Packs made up of Country Gangrel vampires of Native American stock on the Path of Harmony. This is probably a dark secret of the tribes and are the least described in the sourcebooks, but it's been there since the early days. This is the Penumbra of the Gray Squirrels as an &quot;ally&quot; mentioned in the original STs Handbook to the Sabbat. It probably does not extend to all the Sabbat as the group they are encountered with is very particular (and in Revised becomes completely annihilated by other Sabbat), but if you hew to earlier depictions there is something.<br /> <br /> Fifth, there may be Children of Gaia who do not consider vampires who do not detect as a Wyrm as not of the Wyrm. They are much more willing to see new neonates as worthy of support or even protection. This attitude may not apply to all CoG, but there may be enough to make it noteworthy. I think it is really only with this tribe (and probably only with certain camps) that you could have a situation where vampires are truly treated as individuals and could even want to help high Humanity vampires in their struggle to maintain their Humanity. Likewise the Stargazers might be very opened when it comes to particular vampire individuals.<br /> <br /> The other tribes are much more circumspect. Very rare dealings with compromised individuals or packs with most being extremely hostile. But the above tribes' activities with vampires are much more documented.<br /> <br /> Another option is with Ronin, Lost Cubs, and Lunatics. They probably share the same fear as anyone else that vampires might feed on them, but all could be very open to cooperation with individual vampires who don't seem like a threat. It's probably similar with being friends with a known drug addict who is currently clean and sober, but whom you suspect is going to go off the wagon again. If you are a vampire ST looking to include werewolves in a Vampire chronicle, this is probably what I'd use, not someone belonging to a tribe.<br /> <br /> You may also have things like werewolves making promises to certain individuals before they realize what they are (or before they become vampires) and then become trapped by those promises because of their interpretations of Honor Renown, or because their pack or tribal totems require them to act with exceedingly high standards. If a werewolf pack under Falcon made certain promises or oaths to someone later revealed to be a vampire, it doesn't mean those promises no longer applies. It means the werewolf has a very thorny problem in how they balance the competing interests and principles of the Litany.<br /> <br /> Individual vampires might also have various Merits that hide their nature from werewolves, either by making them seem more human or by making them seem more like a werewolf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-01T19:57:09-08:00","id":1527736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1527695-suggested-setting-changes-to-make-crossover-easier?p=1527715#post1527715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Guess I'll move on to urban shadows then. A shame <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. I really wanted to write some crossover groups but people probably wouldn't be interested</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you are looking at this wrong. Don't change the splats from what they are, accept that vampires are monsters, that werewolves are grumpy and mages think they know everything. Systemic changes of the level you are suggesting are messing with the games themselves.<br /> <br /> Now focus on why crossover would work for a given group of indivuals and what kind of stories can they all collaborate in as players. It's fine to setup exceptions with the express purpose of making your own games fun.<br /> <br /> In my experience crossover only really works with a tightly knit pc group that is on a serialised story of the pulpy or urban fantasy ttpe thats not focused on core needs of the splats in question. Sandboxes and highly game specific antagonists are much harder to work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":1182,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","user":"Asmodai","date":". 01-01-2024, 11:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-01T20:17:46-08:00","id":1527740,"title":"","content":"Thanks everyone.<br /> I'll give more in depth answers to your posts soon","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-01T22:51:37-08:00","id":1527749,"title":"","content":"I think the biggest obstacle here is vampires being competitive and moderately paranoid in general. It's not to say that they <i>can't</i> interact with other splats, but they'd have to have a good reason. A shared crisis creating a regionally unusual alliance is definitely possible. That said, of the individual crossovers:<br /> <br /> Werewolves would likely need to see vampires as a lesser threat targeted at a greater evil, and even then that's not guaranteed. One of the defining features of the Garou is a past sense of superiority leading to problems in the present and it's all too easy for them to slip back into old habits. That being said, the Wyrm is very much a fundamental facet of reality. Even Wraiths would arguably ping as of the Wyrm because of their deathly nature giving them a strong affinity for decay. Younger werewolves would likely be more polarized to the idea, some would think Detect Wyrm = Detect Evil because they're new to the situation while others would think it's just sensing natural decay when it's somewhere between the two instead.<br /> <br /> Mages would need some kind of precaution for dealing with vampires, but more than that they'd need something that vampires could offer them that would be worth the risk of an alliance. Innate abilities not subject to paradox would definitely be helpful if facing a wider threat, and information from the past would be extremely valuable.<br /> <br /> Changeling ostensibly have the second greatest potential for overlap, especially in 20th. With regards to vampires: Unseelie Fae already have some familiarity with the nasty side of reality as a necessary part of it, and your earlier observation that vampires should be aware of the Dreaming does have some merit. Sharing research among vampire mystics can be difficult between age torpor and the difficulty in moving between cities, but even that much should offer <i>some</i> insight. Banality in 20th is self-repression rather than <i>stasis</i> per se, so that would allow a greater degree of potential overlap; plus the politics of kithain and vampires are largely self-contained so mutual power plays wouldn't necessarily screw things up too much for the other.<br /> <br /> Changelings and mages could get along, depending, especially with the traditions or a disparate craft; they'd likely avoid the Technocracy like hell though. If changelings interacted with any Technocrats, it would likely be Void Engineers due to their occasional break with orthodoxy to ally with other types of beings and lack of programming.<br /> <br /> Changelings and werewolves are already established to have some overlap via Fianna if I recall, other fera with a mystical bent could absolutely work too.<br /> <br /> Mages and werewolves will have some issues because both have a decent potential for egotistical behavior, but neither are innately offensive to the other save for perhaps the Technocrats being agents of Weaver corruption at best and Wyrm corruption at worst.<br /> <br /> Standard caveat: I could be <i>entirely</i> blowing hot air on this discussion, but there's my two cents.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2532-blitzkitty","name":"BlitzKitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2532_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-02T02:34:42-08:00","id":1527760,"title":"","content":"My assumption with Garou and Cainites was that as the latter are clearly aligned not only to the Wyrm but also the Weaver they were definitely on the list of problems. But the Garou with some level of perspective aren't placing them at the top of the list, they're not causing the biggest issues.<br /> <br /> If the Garou are in active conflict with any of the major conspiracies I'd argue it's the Technocracy, who are responsible for and supporting the system that's causing so much destruction. Although even then they're probably financially backing at least some Glass Walkers.<br /> <br /> But if you really want a setting like WoD where vampires have more crossover potential there were two released by White Wolf and both are quite cool. Admittedly the Uratha in Forsaken 2e definitely hunt all the other splats, but exactly who they go after is very much on a pack by pack basis and the Tribe who include vampires among their dedicated prey are also the one linked to Cunning (and thus likely to form a long term pact of it's more beneficial). Then there's MCWoD which is weirdly good and built assuming that both the 'good' and 'bad' guys have a mixture of different supernatural types. It is 3.5 era d20, but you could port the setting to CofD with minimal difficulty, I think you just need a merit for the Awakened.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-05T10:23:40-08:00","id":1528038,"title":"","content":"I don\u2019t think that there is a single easy answer. It depends on what kind of crossover you\u2019re doing and what sorts of activities or themes take precedence in your crossover. It is primarily a vampire game where, for some reason, a single werewolf becomes enmeshed in vampire politics? Is it a mage focused game where the mages gain a vampire and werewolf ally in their fight against a local Nephandi? What you\u2019re doing with the game is going to determine what setting (or thematic) elements need to be changed if any. <br /> <br /> I don\u2019t think that you can have a crossover without undermining some core themes of at least one of the games involved. If werewolves get help from a local vampire to take down the nearby Pentex factory, there isn\u2019t going to be much focus on Clan intrigue or declining humanity. If a werewolf is hired by the prince for muscle in a war against the Sabbat, then saving the planet and the spiritual battle against the Wyrm isn\u2019t going to receive much focus either. <br /> <br /> I don\u2019t know if a crossover can ever avoid those thematic conflicts even if there is a good excuse for the different creature types to get along and the rules were perfectly balanced. <br /> <br /> If it\u2019s just an anything goes crossover with a Salubri, Sidhe, Glass Walker, Risen, Son of Ether, Mokole, Juicer, and Glitterboy - then theme and setting doesn\u2019t really matter because you\u2019ve kinda abandoned those concepts anyway for wacky adventure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-05T13:56:05-08:00","id":1528056,"title":"","content":"I don't think the themes are that hard to juggle with a big caveat: it can't stretch on too long. One story that's about groups working together towards some goal? You can design that so themes of each line stay relevant. Once you start going for longer though, it either gets forced (because the tricks to keep themes around get redundant fast), or biased towards one set of themes over others. You can try to do some more vampire themed stuff in one story, and then some werewolf themed stuff in the next, and try to share spotlight time as a form of balancing the themes, but it still suffers over time. One big factor is going to be XP, because as characters advance in power, they're expected to advance in their given societies (and that's very necessary for some splats), which will have more drag towards PCs being less crossover friendly even if their personalities and inclinations haven't radically shifted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-05T15:21:21-08:00","id":1528062,"title":"","content":"hi guys,just an update. i've been hired for a thingy so i won't be able to give its thread its due attention. i apologize.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-06T02:01:38-08:00","id":1528090,"title":"","content":"It's probably a feature of my nature as a theoretical fan-boy rather than an experienced player, but a lot of my focus tends to be on the bigger &quot;metaphysical&quot; issues of crossovers in the WoD. I was recently re-reading an old Splat-vs-Splat thread for giggles and it got my mind on the fundamental conflicts between the metaphysical frameworks of Werewolf and Mage, to the point where I kind of wanted to throw up a topic discussing them. This thread seems to be focused a bit more on crunch, but crunch and fluff are interconnected to some extent, so I feel like it's still on topic.<br /> <br /> It's entirely possible that I am missing some things, especially since I'm just throwing ideas out there mostly without a bunch of fact-checking, so I actively invite corrections and feedback.<br /> <br /> But, broadly speaking, it kind of feels like the oWoD throws up between three to five &quot;metaphysical frameworks&quot; which are largely all-encompassing:<br /> <br /> 1) The &quot;Abrahamic&quot; perspective of VtM/DtF<br /> <br /> 2) The &quot;Spiritual Hierarchy&quot; (Gaia + Triat) of WtA<br /> <br /> 3) The &quot;Consensual Reality&quot; of MtA<br /> <br /> 4) The &quot;Celestial Bureacracy&quot; of the &quot;Middle Kingdom,&quot; which manages to blend some aspects of #1 and #2 while also bringing its own baggage to the table<br /> <br /> 5) The &quot;Egyptian Mythos&quot; (Osiris, Horus, Set, etc.), like #4 in being a viewpoint that blends other pre-existing concepts together while also having its own ideas to contribute<br /> <br /> There are plenty of other perspectives; I'm pretty much leaving the basic frameworks of Wraith and Changeling out, for example, because they seem like they are capable of fitting into others without creating fundamental contradictions, paradoxes, or disruption of core themes. But trying to resolve the conflicting lore between these &quot;major&quot; perspectives is often part of the struggle of crossover games. As <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> noted above, it's less of a problem if crossovers are only happening in the short term. But if your crossover games goes on for a while, you need to know what metaphysical framework you are going with in order to decide the best way to handle certain clashes, at least when the &quot;big&quot; questions come up, like when the various &quot;Plot Device&quot; figures in various game-lines might potentially come into conflict.<br /> <br /> The best answers to those questions will ultimately depend on the needs of your players. But as someone who is invested in big WoD crossovers, I'm always interested in trying to find the &quot;golden mean&quot; that does the best job of giving each game-line its due while ultimately creating a comprehensive framework that can guide you on how to fit all the various game-lines together.<br /> <br /> While I do try to do my best to balance things, I do feel like my preferred solution ultimately comes out a bit Mage-centric. Not in the sense that Mages are the most powerful things in existence, but rather in the idea that there is no Sacred Truth that makes any given being or perspective more valid or desirable beyond the purely subjective opinion of the observer. So, for example, Gaia is very big, and Gaia's continued survival is of the utmost importance for anyone who isn't a Wyrm spirit that is willing to roll the dice on finding a better option somewhere in the chaos of the Deep Umbra. But Gaia is ultimately the spirit of This World, not All Nature In Existence. To the extent that Gaia and the Triat are fundamental aspects of the universe, they are like gravity, not morality.<br /> <br /> I don't know if it's impossible to at least mostly protect the themes of each game-line in a crossover-friendly setting. But I do think that something which perfectly balances the needs and perspectives of each game-line is pretty close to a Holy Grail. I like my solution for the most part, though I haven't settled all the answers for myself by any means, but I can see where it would probably not appeal to other folks who want something very different from their crossover games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-06T05:13:01-08:00","id":1528099,"title":"","content":"On the metaphysical level, Demon is really the big problem, because it came in and said, &quot;all the other game lines are wrong, this is the one with the right answers,&quot; and exacerbated Vampire's primary <u>mythology</u> of Noddist revisions to the Abrahamic faith traditions being so tightly bound to Vampire's actual metaphysics (despite lots of attempts by Vampire to point out that the Noddist version has a lot of holes and contradictions in it that make it more a matter of convenience than truth). If Demon didn't decide to go full bore Milton on things, and confirm things like Caine slaying ABel actually happened, Vampire could have stayed vague and easier to slot into the rest via the uncertainty about their true origins.<br /> <br /> Mage is of course an outlier thanks to Consensus, but Consensus doesn't contradict the Umbra-orientd metaphysics that pretty much everyone else uses. The thing about Consensus, is that it only really matters to Mage. While in theory enough effort put into reshaping the Consensus could turn other supernaturals into Bygones and eventually drive them extinct... but most of them have tales about that happening from their own perspectives anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-06T09:49:11-08:00","id":1528110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1527695-suggested-setting-changes-to-make-crossover-easier?p=1528090#post1528090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But Gaia is ultimately the spirit of This World, not All Nature In Existence.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gaia ranges from possibly connected to all things to what the Garou call a much greater cosmic presence. So at the very least, there would be terrible consequences for other worlds, and if Gaia is the latter, there wouldn't be a place to hide.<br /> <br /> (While the Weaver is flat out mad acting like the Infosphere from Futurama, there's probably a reason that there's such a tenacious Weaver presence around the bits of Gaia we're familiar with. The greater cosmic significance hypothesis would mean that the Weaver can learn more about the cosmos by freezing this patch, and it'd get awfully uncomfortable and crystallized everywhere else.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-06T15:06:50-08:00","id":1528125,"title":"","content":"It seems worth noting that the idea of Gaia being the spirit of &quot;All Nature in Existence&quot; is a lot easier to swallow when every game-line besides Demon (and even Demon doesn't exactly contradict) that the WoD takes place in a universe that's really only as big as our Solar system: any attempt to travel beyond our Solar system in the physical realm will lead you into the Deep Umbra, where reality as we know it completely breaks down and there's nothing but endless void (and possibly extremely dangerous beings of cosmic horror stylings). Even the Technocracy hasn't managed to use it's influence on Consensus to push that bubble terribly far despite ensuring that humanity perceives a full universe of galaxies out there that seems ripe for exploration.<br /> <br /> Since the WoD generally posits that it's universe is much, much smaller than the observable universe in our true reality, it's a lot easier for Gaia to be a combination of the spirit of Earth, and the spirit of the cosmos... there is far less of a distinction in the WoD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-07T12:26:56-08:00","id":1528160,"title":"","content":"I've always felt Sabbat chronicles offer the most possibilities for constructive interactions between vampires and the Garou. This is something you do see get explored in some official material, sometimes \u2013 say, <i>Montreal by Night'</i>s Country Gangrel <i>antitribu</i> and her werewolf pals in the forests of northern Quebec. I associate the Loyalist faction of the Sabbat in particular with violent anti-colonial movements and anarcho-primitivism; there could be loads of potential for thematic cross-over with <i>Werewolf</i> there. Limiting the only werewolf variety vampires can interact with without getting BTFO'd to Black Spiral Dancers seems like a tremendous waste of potential.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28177-gamiem","name":"gamiem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28177_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-08T07:39:36-08:00","id":1528209,"title":"","content":"Sorry for the delayed response! I've been kind of busy the last few days, and I knew I'd need a little time to think about my reply.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1527695-suggested-setting-changes-to-make-crossover-easier?p=1528110#post1528110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gaia ranges from possibly connected to all things to what the Garou call a much greater cosmic presence. So at the very least, there would be terrible consequences for other worlds, and if Gaia is the latter, there wouldn't be a place to hide.<br /> <br /> (While the Weaver is flat out mad acting like the Infosphere from Futurama, there's probably a reason that there's such a tenacious Weaver presence around the bits of Gaia we're familiar with. The greater cosmic significance hypothesis would mean that the Weaver can learn more about the cosmos by freezing this patch, and it'd get awfully uncomfortable and crystallized everywhere else.)</div> </div> </div> </div>You have a lot more experience with Werewolf than me, so correct me if I'm wrong, but it has always seemed to me like the particulars around what Gaia is or what her agenda tends to be kept vague and ineffable. Which makes sense for some narrative reasons, like how Eshtarra refuses to act as a totem to keep Garou from thinking that Gaia Herself is personally rubber-stamping everything they do. But the result is that it seems to me like any and all of the possibilities you've raised above are open for debate if they aren't willing to settle them in a concrete fashion. But then, there's something that I'll be saying below which may address the disagreement here somewhat.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1527695-suggested-setting-changes-to-make-crossover-easier?p=1528125#post1528125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems worth noting that the idea of Gaia being the spirit of &quot;All Nature in Existence&quot; is a lot easier to swallow when every game-line besides Demon (and even Demon doesn't exactly contradict) that the WoD takes place in a universe that's really only as big as our Solar system: any attempt to travel beyond our Solar system in the physical realm will lead you into the Deep Umbra, where reality as we know it completely breaks down and there's nothing but endless void (and possibly extremely dangerous beings of cosmic horror stylings). Even the Technocracy hasn't managed to use it's influence on Consensus to push that bubble terribly far despite ensuring that humanity perceives a full universe of galaxies out there that seems ripe for exploration.<br /> <br /> Since the WoD generally posits that it's universe is much, much smaller than the observable universe in our true reality, it's a lot easier for Gaia to be a combination of the spirit of Earth, and the spirit of the cosmos... there is far less of a distinction in the WoD.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is actually the main thing that I'm talking about. I'm not so much arguing that Gaia isn't extremely important to this little cosmos, a tiny bubble of existence floating around in the chaos of the Deep Umbra, but rather the idea that this cosmos itself is just one random universe, and there could be more out there. I'm arguing against Gaia's importance on a Multiversal Scale. Which seems a little big for WoD, but the notion does come up in a couple of places. Firstly in the part of the scenario of Ascension where Tychoides decides to jump ship for a different Reality, and also in the minor groups among the Garou and Fera who search for a possible new home in the Deep Umbra. It matters to me, in this case, because it helps to establish the foundational principles for my personal WoD canon that then inform how I resolve other issues going forward.<br /> <br /> I remember someone describing the idea of abandoning Gaia like that as a very &quot;Elon Musk&quot; maneuver, and I always really enjoyed that framing because it felt like it perfectly sums it up. Both in the sense of how it involves a massive denial or abandonment of any moral obligation or responsibility to the Earth or the majority of people who are going to be left to die, and in how desperate and dangerous such a plan ultimately is. But if it's the only option realistically available? I think that creates an interesting tension to explore, the kind of story where the right answer will at least somewhat depend on the opinions of the PCs.<br /> <br /> I almost forgot, but a related idea that my brain has gotten onto is the relationship between Gaia and the Triat in the &quot;spiritual hierarchy.&quot; As noted above, Gaia's particular nature is left purposefully vague, and even whether or not she is equal to, or outranks even, the Triat is left ambiguous. Part of my interest in diminishing Gaia's importance probably partly comes from my personal canon leaning towards the idea that the Triat are the Bigger Fish in that scenario. But this conversation has gotten me considering alternatives. Initially, the fact that the Shenti are found out in the Deep Umbra inclined me to see the forces of the Triat as operating on a scale bigger than the Universe of the setting, whereas Gaia would be, at most, that one Universe. But I have started to ponder the idea that the Shenti may still be loosely &quot;attached&quot; or &quot;connected&quot; to this reality, somehow, and that perhaps different balances of spiritual forces might be found in a different Universe.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-09T11:34:06-08:00","id":1528273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1527695-suggested-setting-changes-to-make-crossover-easier?p=1528209#post1528209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry for the delayed response! I've been kind of busy the last few days, and I knew I'd need a little time to think about my reply.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> You have a lot more experience with Werewolf than me, so correct me if I'm wrong, but it has always seemed to me like the particulars around what Gaia is or what her agenda tends to be kept vague and ineffable. Which makes sense for some narrative reasons, like how Eshtarra refuses to act as a totem to keep Garou from thinking that Gaia Herself is personally rubber-stamping everything they do. But the result is that it seems to me like any and all of the possibilities you've raised above are open for debate if they aren't willing to settle them in a concrete fashion. But then, there's something that I'll be saying below which may address the disagreement here somewhat.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would characterize it as &quot;broad strokes&quot; rather than wholly ineffable. Gaia wants the Changing Breeds to do what she made them to, but there's a rather wide open range of ways to do this. Having the Gnosis trait generally also means that Her presence is always apparent, even if it's not a clean cut thing.<br /> <br /> However, it isn't open for debate. The W:tA core stated out of character that Gaia is way bigger than the planet alone (W20 page 307); any material to the contrary tends to get only as much word count as it takes to introduce the possibility, and then it's gone, and the game gets back to its default assumption. The Tellurian is the word used to reference a level of organization larger than this, which includes other realities. Garou might be getting slightly ahead of themselves to conflate the two, but they wouldn't necessarily be wrong to do it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is actually the main thing that I'm talking about. I'm not so much arguing that Gaia isn't extremely important to this little cosmos, a tiny bubble of existence floating around in the chaos of the Deep Umbra, but rather the idea that this cosmos itself is just one random universe, and there could be more out there. I'm arguing against Gaia's importance on a Multiversal Scale. Which seems a little big for WoD, but the notion does come up in a couple of places. Firstly in the part of the scenario of Ascension where Tychoides decides to jump ship for a different Reality, and also in the minor groups among the Garou and Fera who search for a possible new home in the Deep Umbra. It matters to me, in this case, because it helps to establish the foundational principles for my personal WoD canon that then inform how I resolve other issues going forward. </div> </div> </div>If you accept this proposition it de-values W:tA so heavily that it might as well just throw it to the side. It's about actually caring and unironically feeling it. Cutting and running is not part of the plan, or any plan; there's nowhere to run, and you're going to be making your stand here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I remember someone describing the idea of abandoning Gaia like that as a very &quot;Elon Musk&quot; maneuver, and I always really enjoyed that framing because it felt like it perfectly sums it up. Both in the sense of how it involves a massive denial or abandonment of any moral obligation or responsibility to the Earth or the majority of people who are going to be left to die, and in how desperate and dangerous such a plan ultimately is. But if it's the only option realistically available? I think that creates an interesting tension to explore, the kind of story where the right answer will at least somewhat depend on the opinions of the PCs. </div> </div> </div>As noted, it was never available. That's completely out of theme, and you'd have to hack out an entirely new game to cover it being a possible route, rather than what happened in canon, where all the alternate spirit-questing Wagnerians came back and said &quot;No other Gaias, fam,&quot; while meanwhile a bunch of Nuwisha returned to Earth heavily wounded and near-death croaking out warnings of only death waiting in the furthest reaches of the Umbra before expiring.<br /> <br /> You can run, but you'll only die tired, because after the Midnight Shadows (see Apocalypse) are done with the coyotes, they're going to sweep back for <i>you</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I almost forgot, but a related idea that my brain has gotten onto is the relationship between Gaia and the Triat in the &quot;spiritual hierarchy.&quot; As noted above, Gaia's particular nature is left purposefully vague, and even whether or not she is equal to, or outranks even, the Triat is left ambiguous. Part of my interest in diminishing Gaia's importance probably partly comes from my personal canon leaning towards the idea that the Triat are the Bigger Fish in that scenario. But this conversation has gotten me considering alternatives. Initially, the fact that the Shenti are found out in the Deep Umbra inclined me to see the forces of the Triat as operating on a scale bigger than the Universe of the setting, whereas Gaia would be, at most, that one Universe. But I have started to ponder the idea that the Shenti may still be loosely &quot;attached&quot; or &quot;connected&quot; to this reality, somehow, and that perhaps different balances of spiritual forces might be found in a different Universe. </div> </div> </div>The Shenti aren't anywhere nearly distant enough to qualify as other universes, at least not in W:tA, and especially not by the time the Apocalypse is revving up and Malfeas moves from the Deep Umbra to the Near Umbra (which is also where Flux is; I'm not sure where the hell Autochthonia is supposed to be in W:tA, it doesn't get mentioned very often, but if it's in the Aetherial opposite Earth, then it, too, is in the Near Umbra and not the Deep Umbra). The Mage metaphysical trinity is also not the same thing as the Triat, because the MT doesn't actively do much, but the Triat surely does act, with each Supernal of it acting to further their ends, possibly except for the Wyld, which is frequently characterized as just there, doing its thing to the best of its abilities regardless of its surroundings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-10T16:34:43-08:00","id":1528343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1527695-suggested-setting-changes-to-make-crossover-easier?p=1528273#post1528273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would characterize it as &quot;broad strokes&quot; rather than wholly ineffable. Gaia wants the Changing Breeds to do what she made them to, but there's a rather wide open range of ways to do this. Having the Gnosis trait generally also means that Her presence is always apparent, even if it's not a clean cut thing.<br /> <br /> However, it isn't open for debate. The W:tA core stated out of character that Gaia is way bigger than the planet alone (W20 page 307); any material to the contrary tends to get only as much word count as it takes to introduce the possibility, and then it's gone, and the game gets back to its default assumption. The Tellurian is the word used to reference a level of organization larger than this, which includes other realities. Garou might be getting slightly ahead of themselves to conflate the two, but they wouldn't necessarily be wrong to do it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I meant to check the W20 citation you provided before responding. But the week has turned out a bit busier than I had planned, and I don't want to put off replying again. So I will just thank you for the information for the time being and maybe follow up on that point later when I've had time to check the details <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1527695-suggested-setting-changes-to-make-crossover-easier?p=1528273#post1528273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you accept this proposition it de-values W:tA so heavily that it might as well just throw it to the side. It's about actually caring and unironically feeling it. Cutting and running is not part of the plan, or any plan; there's nowhere to run, and you're going to be making your stand here.<br /> <br /> <br /> As noted, it was never available. That's completely out of theme, and you'd have to hack out an entirely new game to cover it being a possible route, rather than what happened in canon, where all the alternate spirit-questing Wagnerians came back and said &quot;No other Gaias, fam,&quot; while meanwhile a bunch of Nuwisha returned to Earth heavily wounded and near-death croaking out warnings of only death waiting in the furthest reaches of the Umbra before expiring.<br /> <br /> You can run, but you'll only die tired, because after the Midnight Shadows (see Apocalypse) are done with the coyotes, they're going to sweep back for <i>you</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like both of these points are somewhat addressed by the fact that we're explicitly discussing all of this in the context of Crossover.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't propose this kind of background for a &quot;pure&quot; WtA game, with players looking to explore the core themes of WtA. It's being proposed in a discussion of how to make crossover work in the wider World of Darkness when the metaphysical assumptions of the various games profoundly clash with one another. Trying to find a Big WoD crossover setting that doesn't require some of the game-lines getting thrown under the bus a bit is kind of a Holy Grail. And having not achieved that, my interpretation kind of shafts Werewolf because the idea of the Garou being Unquestionably Correct on at least most of the big cosmological questions is intensely uninteresting to me. My preferred themes are more along the lines of Nihilism/Existentialism and Cosmic Horror, and every game-line's premises are incorporated or discarded with those interests in mind.<br /> <br /> Now, whether or not that means that I should just &quot;throw Werewolf to the side&quot; kind of depends on what you mean by that proposition. If you simply mean throwing aside a lot of the core themes and conceits of the setting, then yeah, that is precisely what I am doing, and I've acknowledged it from the start as something I'm doing in the context of a Crossover conversation.<br /> <br /> If, however, your argument is that I should not bother trying to incorporate the Garou, Triat, Gaia, etc., into a Big WoD Crossover setting, that I should just settle for &quot;Lupines&quot; or some nonsense instead, then my response would be to say that I'd be doing that from the start if that was what interested me. I actually find a lot of stuff about Werewolf interesting. But I find it more interesting when you actually leave room for them to be seriously wrong about something fundamental, not just whether or not they are pursuing their Unquestionable Crusade in the most effective manner. I know that they feel the Truth of it in their bones, and I don't care, and I am actively eager to pick at the flaws in that kind of reasoning. I don't think that I have to believe their Lore belongs on a pedestal to enjoy having them as part of my game.<br /> <br /> As just one example, I think having the option to &quot;jump ship&quot; potentially opens up more interesting options for a story about &quot;actually caring and unironically feeling it,&quot; because having the option to run and choosing to stand your ground anyways shows more genuine commitment to your ideals, it seems to me, than fighting a last stand because you don't even have another option. I'm not saying that the desperation of having nowhere else to run isn't a good story element, but you can get rid of it and still leave room for a good Werewolf story, I think.<br /> <br /> I do try to undercut the themes of other game-lines as well. My preferred approach is to try and humble every Splat to some extent or another. But yeah, my preferences do tend to lean especially far aware from the typical themes of Werewolf, so I understand my personal ideas not being especially appealing to Werewolf fans.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1527695-suggested-setting-changes-to-make-crossover-easier?p=1528273#post1528273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Shenti aren't anywhere nearly distant enough to qualify as other universes, at least not in W:tA, and especially not by the time the Apocalypse is revving up and Malfeas moves from the Deep Umbra to the Near Umbra (which is also where Flux is; I'm not sure where the hell Autochthonia is supposed to be in W:tA, it doesn't get mentioned very often, but if it's in the Aetherial opposite Earth, then it, too, is in the Near Umbra and not the Deep Umbra). The Mage metaphysical trinity is also not the same thing as the Triat, because the MT doesn't actively do much, but the Triat surely does act, with each Supernal of it acting to further their ends, possibly except for the Wyld, which is frequently characterized as just there, doing its thing to the best of its abilities regardless of its surroundings.</div> </div> </div> </div>To clarify, I wasn't talking about the idea of Shenti as Other Universes. What I meant was more a question of whether or not the Shenti are only a part of This Universe (the WoD setting), or if they/the Triat are a component of the wider Multiverse/the Deep Umbra. If there are Other Universes hidden way out somewhere in the Deep Umbra, would they necessary split between Creation, Stasis, and Entropy, or would there be room for fundamentally different spiritual energies, with different relationships to each other, to exist? Again, extremely theoretical question. I just tend to approach this stuff like a metaphysician, trying to start from fundamentals and build up from there.<br /> <br /> Obviously a Storyteller could go either way. But I thought I remembered all of the Shenti being located beyond the Membrane in the Deep Umbra, so that potentially implied that the first answer might be more correct, and that the Triat might therefore be a more prominent aspect of the wider cosmos.<br /> <br /> Regarding the split between the Trinity and the Triat, I mostly just imagine it as the difference between there River and the Spirit of the River. The two are connected, but the spiritual aspect is more active and &quot;aware.&quot; And the Triat's influence tends to be overlooked and underestimated by most Mages, who aren't really the centre of existence that they like to imagine themselves as, either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-10T18:54:27-08:00","id":1528346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1527695-suggested-setting-changes-to-make-crossover-easier?p=1528343#post1528343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I feel like both of these points are somewhat addressed by the fact that we're explicitly discussing all of this in the context of Crossover.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't propose this kind of background for a &quot;pure&quot; WtA game, with players looking to explore the core themes of WtA. It's being proposed in a discussion of how to make crossover work in the wider World of Darkness when the metaphysical assumptions of the various games profoundly clash with one another. Trying to find a Big WoD crossover setting that doesn't require some of the game-lines getting thrown under the bus a bit is kind of a Holy Grail. And having not achieved that, my interpretation kind of shafts Werewolf because the idea of the Garou being Unquestionably Correct on at least most of the big cosmological questions is intensely uninteresting to me. My preferred themes are more along the lines of Nihilism/Existentialism and Cosmic Horror, and every game-line's premises are incorporated or discarded with those interests in mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the other hand, full-spectrum WoD crossover is technically impossible. Mage and Werewolf are incompatible in their assumptions of how the Umbrae work; for example, you've been referencing the Deep Umbra for several posts, and I'm not sure if you mean what Werewolf still counts as physical outer space or what it actually refers to as the Deep Umbra, a second Umbra behind the Membrane that's accessed only via Anchorheads, for the most part.<br /> <br /> The differences don't stop there, either, but to sum up some other important and largely irreconcilable differences, in Mage, humanity is the most important thing in the cosmos. In Werewolf, they're another animal, one that climbed on top of a pedestal that they have no business being astride.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Now, whether or not that means that I should just &quot;throw Werewolf to the side&quot; kind of depends on what you mean by that proposition. If you simply mean throwing aside a lot of the core themes and conceits of the setting, then yeah, that is precisely what I am doing, and I've acknowledged it from the start as something I'm doing in the context of a Crossover conversation.<br /> <br /> If, however, your argument is that I should not bother trying to incorporate the Garou, Triat, Gaia, etc., into a Big WoD Crossover setting, that I should just settle for &quot;Lupines&quot; or some nonsense instead, then my response would be to say that I'd be doing that from the start if that was what interested me. I actually find a lot of stuff about Werewolf interesting. But I find it more interesting when you actually leave room for them to be seriously wrong about something fundamental, not just whether or not they are pursuing their Unquestionable Crusade in the most effective manner. I know that they feel the Truth of it in their bones, and I don't care, and I am actively eager to pick at the flaws in that kind of reasoning. I don't think that I have to believe their Lore belongs on a pedestal to enjoy having them as part of my game. </div> </div> </div>The problem being that this is how you get W5, i.e. a vague mess that isn't sure whether the Garou should even exist, and often edges out on trying to say that they shouldn't. I don't think of the lore of being on a pedestal as much as it is very basic and simple, and something that you can zoom in or out of as is needed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As just one example, I think having the option to &quot;jump ship&quot; potentially opens up more interesting options for a story about &quot;actually caring and unironically feeling it,&quot; because having the option to run and choosing to stand your ground anyways shows more genuine commitment to your ideals, it seems to me, than fighting a last stand because you don't even have another option. I'm not saying that the desperation of having nowhere else to run isn't a good story element, but you can get rid of it and still leave room for a good Werewolf story, I think. </div> </div> </div>Mostly in historical settings, or modern settings where it doesn't assume that the Apocalypse is already on.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I do try to undercut the themes of other game-lines as well. My preferred approach is to try and humble every Splat to some extent or another. But yeah, my preferences do tend to lean especially far aware from the typical themes of Werewolf, so I understand my personal ideas not being especially appealing to Werewolf fans. </div> </div> </div>In the end, every game says that it screwed up the worst or is the worst because of a curse, and that would probably have to be dialed back all around in order to avoid making one game having screwed up too hard or being more responsible over all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> To clarify, I wasn't talking about the idea of Shenti as Other Universes. What I meant was more a question of whether or not the Shenti are only a part of This Universe (the WoD setting), or if they/the Triat are a component of the wider Multiverse/the Deep Umbra. If there are Other Universes hidden way out somewhere in the Deep Umbra, would they necessary split between Creation, Stasis, and Entropy, or would there be room for fundamentally different spiritual energies, with different relationships to each other, to exist? Again, extremely theoretical question. I just tend to approach this stuff like a metaphysician, trying to start from fundamentals and build up from there. </div> </div> </div>The Triat compose reality. The Wyrm is a third of reality, the Weaver is another third, and the Wyld the last piece. There isn't room for different spiritual energies <u>at this level of organization</u> because of how basic and primal they're supposed to be.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Obviously a Storyteller could go either way. But I thought I remembered all of the Shenti being located beyond the Membrane in the Deep Umbra, so that potentially implied that the first answer might be more correct, and that the Triat might therefore be a more prominent aspect of the wider cosmos. </div> </div> </div>Only Malfeas, mostly on account of how it has &quot;scar tissue&quot; surrounding it as the place where the Wyrm was bound into the Pattern Web by the Weaver. Again, though, during the End Times, it moved into the Near Umbra.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Regarding the split between the Trinity and the Triat, I mostly just imagine it as the difference between there River and the Spirit of the River. The two are connected, but the spiritual aspect is more active and &quot;aware.&quot; And the Triat's influence tends to be overlooked and underestimated by most Mages, who aren't really the centre of existence that they like to imagine themselves as, either. </div> </div> </div>In Werewolf, the spirit of the river <i>is</i> the river. If it's killed, the river dries up. Changing that will basically get you nega-Werewolf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-11T08:29:16-08:00","id":1528360,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25886\" data-vbnamecard=\"25886\">Kharnov</a> I think the additional problem here is that some ideas are so incompatible that everyone will have to make their own decisions on whats actually true. This means that there is no way to make them all compatible in an objective manner.<br /> <br /> You see Werewolf's assumptions as easy to neglect and justify in other contexts. If someone else runs their crossover they might consider KotE and Werewolf to be ultimatley correct and just consider Demon and Mage as hopped up fever dreams.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-11T09:58:41-08:00","id":1528362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1527695-suggested-setting-changes-to-make-crossover-easier?p=1528346#post1528346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the other hand, full-spectrum WoD crossover is technically impossible. Mage and Werewolf are incompatible in their assumptions of how the Umbrae work; for example, you've been referencing the Deep Umbra for several posts, and I'm not sure if you mean what Werewolf still counts as physical outer space or what it actually refers to as the Deep Umbra, a second Umbra behind the Membrane that's accessed only via Anchorheads, for the most part.<br /> <br /> The differences don't stop there, either, but to sum up some other important and largely irreconcilable differences, in Mage, humanity is the most important thing in the cosmos. In Werewolf, they're another animal, one that climbed on top of a pedestal that they have no business being astride.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd have to go back and read it again, but I remembered Mage using similar rules for Anchorheads and the Membrane, even if Mages had a bit more flexibility in pushing through on their own. The main difference that I recall is simply the line of where the Deep Umbra starts. Now, if there are some serious problems that result for the major themes of Werewolf by, for example, leaning on the Mage interpretation, I'd very much like to hear them. But I didn't bother talking about it because that's never struck me as one of the major problems to resolve. If Werewolf actually did more with outer space, maybe I'd worry more about stepping on their toes. But AFAIK the Garou are only going up into space when they're in the Aetherial Realm, which kind of operates by its own separate rules. I'm not saying you don't need to settle some issues, but they aren't the tough nuts to crack from my perspective.<br /> <br /> Mages are a cosmic accident with an inflated notion of their own importance, who are just as liable to blow themselves up as get themselves swallowed by some nasty Eldritch Abomination.<br /> <br /> Or rather, that's the relatively straightforward answer I have as an alternative to &quot;Mage is humanity-centric.&quot; I kind of agree, inasmuch as I find Mages to be an almost perfect analogy for some of the worst excesses of humanity itself; a relatively young species that has been gifted with perceptions and powers that far exceed their ability to wield wisely. That would actually mesh with the Werewolf opinion pretty well, it seems.<br /> <br /> If &quot;technically impossible&quot; means a Crossover that will always 100% faithfully respect the source material and themes of every game-line included, I have never disagreed with the claim that it's impossible. Or at least, I've referred to it as a Utopian ideal to be chased after, but probably never achieved, lol. Where I'm disagreeing is with the idea that Crossover therefore becomes pointless, that the &quot;purity&quot; of each game-line is so important that you can't make whatever changes are necessary to get the story that you want. They're rulebooks, not a Bible.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm going to pre-empt the &quot;Well why are you even using World of Darkness then?&quot; argument. I like the background mythology; I just don't think it all has to be True for it to be Interesting. I like the idea that all of these groups fervently believe in the Truth that they are chasing after, that the world is so full of mystery and horror that entire societies of mystics and monsters can sit right next to each other and barely know anything because they're too wrapped up in their own issues, and because everyone's an untrustworthy asshole.<br /> <br /> While it can make it difficult to try and fit everything together at times, I really love the way that the writers aggressively insist on keeping so much of the mystery in the world by refusing to give canon answers to many issues and forcing you to come up with your own solutions.<br /> <br /> And honestly, I love the crazy over-the-top world created by throwing all of the Splats and the kitchen sink into one tiny little box together, and just watching the chaos.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1527695-suggested-setting-changes-to-make-crossover-easier?p=1528346#post1528346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem being that this is how you get W5, i.e. a vague mess that isn't sure whether the Garou should even exist, and often edges out on trying to say that they shouldn't. I don't think of the lore of being on a pedestal as much as it is very basic and simple, and something that you can zoom in or out of as is needed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like this is a kind of spurious comparison. W5 fails as a &quot;pure&quot; Werewolf game. And its failings, in my opinion, go quite a ways beyond the kinds of changes you need to make to provide an entertaining Crossover game in pre-X5 editions. Trying to apply the same standards is unreasonable, as far as I'm concerned. I'm being upfront about the fact that this interpretation is not for Werewolf purists. Or (insert-gameline) purists of any kind. It's a Crossover, and aside from my personal preferences in taste, it's primary job is to make the necessary compromises.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1527695-suggested-setting-changes-to-make-crossover-easier?p=1528346#post1528346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mostly in historical settings, or modern settings where it doesn't assume that the Apocalypse is already on.</div> </div> </div> </div>This really feels like a fundamental disagreement on taste. I don't accept that having the Apocalypse be imminent inevitably diminishes the dramatic value/tension that comes from the option to run. Think of Sam's speech at the end of the film version of The Two Towers. Having the end staring you in the face, and still choosing to press on, is an awesome mood, I think.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1527695-suggested-setting-changes-to-make-crossover-easier?p=1528346#post1528346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the end, every game says that it screwed up the worst or is the worst because of a curse, and that would probably have to be dialed back all around in order to avoid making one game having screwed up too hard or being more responsible over all.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I'd need a bit more specific examples to say more about how I'd address the issues, but I do broadly agree that you can't just take the problems as presented in each individual game-line and try and force them to fit together. A fair amount of revision is necessary. But it's doable, and even enjoyable at times.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1527695-suggested-setting-changes-to-make-crossover-easier?p=1528346#post1528346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Triat compose reality. The Wyrm is a third of reality, the Weaver is another third, and the Wyld the last piece. There isn't room for different spiritual energies <u>at this level of organization</u> because of how basic and primal they're supposed to be.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, there is theoretically room for one more layer down, what would be called Prime in Mage: the absolute base level monism, the stuff that can be literally anything. What I'm discussing is the idea that said &quot;Universal Substance&quot; could express itself in different ways. I personally kind of prefer a dualism of Change/Stasis (Order/Chaos also works, but has a lot of other baggage attached I kind of like to avoid). But I'm not at all opposed to having the Triat representing the most basic functions of reality, either. It just has implications that need to be worked through.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1527695-suggested-setting-changes-to-make-crossover-easier?p=1528346#post1528346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Only Malfeas, mostly on account of how it has &quot;scar tissue&quot; surrounding it as the place where the Wyrm was bound into the Pattern Web by the Weaver. Again, though, during the End Times, it moved into the Near Umbra.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough. Also, quick question: is &quot;Shenti&quot; a term that originated in Werewolf or Mage? It'd been a little while since I looked at the concept, and I initially assumed Werewolf, but the wiki kind of makes it sound like more of a Mage concept. (I know the wiki isn't great; I use it as a quick reference and a starting point for deeper research on a topic.)<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1527695-suggested-setting-changes-to-make-crossover-easier?p=1528346#post1528346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In Werewolf, the spirit of the river <i>is</i> the river. If it's killed, the river dries up. Changing that will basically get you nega-Werewolf.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure if we're even in disagreement here, aside from maybe some semantics? Or there's a lot more about the differences between Triat and Trinity that I am missing.<br /> <br /> I would essentially agree with what you've characterized here: To use one example, Stasis is the River, and the Weaver is the River-spirit. I am 100% in agreement that they are fundamentally intertwined and that something affecting one will have profound consequences on the other. If you kill the Weaver, you destroy Stasis, and Reality itself probably collapses in on itself in the process.<br /> <br /> But while they are inextricably bound together, I do feel like there's an extent to which you can speak about them as separate things. The Body and the Soul are tightly bound together, and anything you do to one part will impact the whole. But even as they are part of the same whole, they possess certain aspects and traits which are radically different from one another, and you can talk about those particular components separate from each other while still acknowledging that they are connected.<br /> <br /> The fact that the Gauntlet exists, and divides the spiritual and material parts of reality, suggests to me that there is some value in discussing them as distinct from each other, even if you think they are ultimately connected at the root.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, I got around to checking W20 307, and I feel like the fact that it explicitly mentions the existence of the Tellurian as something which is supposed to be bigger than Gaia kind of supports the argument I'm going for. But I also feel like I might need to clarify something: I'm not rejecting the idea that Gaia's influence extends beyond the Material World and the Penumbra, into the Near Umbra and the various Realms contained within. I am including those within my concept of &quot;This World&quot; and I apologize if failing to make that clear has caused any communication issues.<br /> <br /> What I'm focused on is what's being hit on by the conflict between Werewolf and Mage theories of the universe. If you accept the Werewolf framing, that there is an infinite material universe entirely separate from the Deep Umbra, then you leave room for the idea that there is life out on those other worlds, and that Gaia is the Mother-Goddess of them as well. I'm rejecting that premise.<br /> <br /> But I did recently run into another tidbit that forces me to acknowledge that I'm fighting against the current in Werewolf more than I initially realized; while reading about the planetary Incarna, I encountered the idea that Luna is supposed to be the spirit of ALL Moons, while Sohkta/Phoebe is just the Incarna of Earth's Moon. Which would also conflict with the concept I'm pitching.<br /> <br /> <br /> The title of this thread is &quot;Suggested setting changes to make crossover easier.&quot; That Crossover is desirable is built into the premise of the discussion. I'd love help finding and addressing the challenges that come up in Crossover. But simply arguing that Crossover is a bad idea in the first place seems kind of contrarian when the whole conversation is about wanting to play Crossover games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","user":"Kharnov","date":". 01-11-2024, 01:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-11T10:09:49-08:00","id":1528363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1527695-suggested-setting-changes-to-make-crossover-easier?p=1528360#post1528360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25886\" data-vbnamecard=\"25886\">Kharnov</a> I think the additional problem here is that some ideas are so incompatible that everyone will have to make their own decisions on whats actually true. This means that there is no way to make them all compatible in an objective manner.<br /> <br /> You see Werewolf's assumptions as easy to neglect and justify in other contexts. If someone else runs their crossover they might consider KotE and Werewolf to be ultimatley correct and just consider Demon and Mage as hopped up fever dreams.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, I got too focused on the other message, forgot to include my reply to this!<br /> <br /> Short answer: Yes?<br /> <br /> I have no problem with other people having different interpretations; I'd actively encourage it, even. It's a game, and everyone should engage with it in the way that is the most enjoyable for them <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> As I said, I'm being very upfront about the fact that this is my personal Crossover-canon, that it is shaped by my particular tastes and interests, and that certain game-lines will get to be more &quot;right&quot; than others, at least about certain things.<br /> <br /> One example: I actually take the Fera account of prehistory as mostly accurate. The Dragon-Kings. The Wonder-Work. All of that is at least broadly canon in my head. The Garou are at least somewhat correct in the fact that the world has been running like this since time immemorial. Humanity is just this weird problem that suddenly emerged and has mostly made everything worse.<br /> <br /> One of the biggest struggles I'm having right now is with the idea that THIS may have actually been the origin of the War in Heaven: the Fallen are the Angels that are essentially Human-supremacist, who wanted to raise them over the rest of Creation, while God/the loyal Angels wanted humanity to take it slow so that they could learn how to live in balance with the rest of the world. But the extent to which Demon binds itself to Christian mythology makes it a bit tricky, without leaning REALLY HARD on the idea that the Fallens' memories are messed up by their time in the Abyss and the intermingling with their human hosts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-11T11:05:33-08:00","id":1528373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1527695-suggested-setting-changes-to-make-crossover-easier?p=1528362#post1528362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd have to go back and read it again, but I remembered Mage using similar rules for Anchorheads and the Membrane, even if Mages had a bit more flexibility in pushing through on their own. The main difference that I recall is simply the line of where the Deep Umbra starts. Now, if there are some serious problems that result for the major themes of Werewolf by, for example, leaning on the Mage interpretation, I'd very much like to hear them. But I didn't bother talking about it because that's never struck me as one of the major problems to resolve. If Werewolf actually did more with outer space, maybe I'd worry more about stepping on their toes. But AFAIK the Garou are only going up into space when they're in the Aetherial Realm, which kind of operates by its own separate rules. I'm not saying you don't need to settle some issues, but they aren't the tough nuts to crack from my perspective.</div> </div> </div> </div>The business with MIR wouldn't be possible in W:tA if space and the Umbra were one and the same, because it involved BSDs hiding out in the spiritual shadow of it while spooking the cosmonauts from time to time. With the rising trend of commerical spaceflight, Garou are also incredibly likely to either hitch rides or go to the Aetherial Realm and head, say, Musk's plans for Mars off at the pass by stepping sideways into the habitat modules and making sure that Mars stays very, very red.<br /> <br /> There's also a plot hook in the Revised W:tA Storyteller's Handbook involving aliens from space that have nothing to do with the Umbra, and I'm not willing to dispense with that as a potential plot seed. That's XCOM, baby!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Mages are a cosmic accident with an inflated notion of their own importance, who are just as liable to blow themselves up as get themselves swallowed by some nasty Eldritch Abomination.<br /> <br /> Or rather, that's the relatively straightforward answer I have as an alternative to &quot;Mage is humanity-centric.&quot; I kind of agree, inasmuch as I find Mages to be an almost perfect analogy for some of the worst excesses of humanity itself; a relatively young species that has been gifted with perceptions and powers that far exceed their ability to wield wisely. That would actually mesh with the Werewolf opinion pretty well, it seems.<br /> <br /> If &quot;technically impossible&quot; means a Crossover that will always 100% faithfully respect the source material and themes of every game-line included, I have never disagreed with the claim that it's impossible. Or at least, I've referred to it as a Utopian ideal to be chased after, but probably never achieved, lol. Where I'm disagreeing is with the idea that Crossover therefore becomes pointless, that the &quot;purity&quot; of each game-line is so important that you can't make whatever changes are necessary to get the story that you want. They're rulebooks, not a Bible. </div> </div> </div>They were also (I suppose one could say unhelpfully) written that way entirely on purpose. Except when they weren't, like with Mummy 2nd edition.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm going to pre-empt the &quot;Well why are you even using World of Darkness then?&quot; argument. I like the background mythology; I just don't think it all has to be True for it to be Interesting. I like the idea that all of these groups fervently believe in the Truth that they are chasing after, that the world is so full of mystery and horror that entire societies of mystics and monsters can sit right next to each other and barely know anything because they're too wrapped up in their own issues, and because everyone's an untrustworthy asshole.<br /> <br /> While it can make it difficult to try and fit everything together at times, I really love the way that the writers aggressively insist on keeping so much of the mystery in the world by refusing to give canon answers to many issues and forcing you to come up with your own solutions. </div> </div> </div>I could do without any of Vampire's metaplot style, frankly. &quot;Watch while you're helpless to do anything, pathetic neonates!&quot; can go die.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And honestly, I love the crazy over-the-top world created by throwing all of the Splats and the kitchen sink into one tiny little box together, and just watching the chaos. </div> </div> </div>Some games managed to weld it together better than others. KotE, while being saddled with a heavy orientalist bent, had a construction mashing together the Middle and Dark Umbrae that didn't manage to step on anyone's toes. Regrettably, it also had Blood and Silk, which decided that it needed to push the Hakken as the only Garou other than the Stargazers in the Beast Courts. And which were known by that name, all the way back during the earliest part of the Chinese history, a good two thousand years before it would have made any sense at all (two strikes for being Japanese in ancient China before the Yayoi had even finished their migration to Japan, and also because Buddhism didn't become a thing until several centuries BCE, the Virtues of which are what the Hakken were named for).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I feel like this is a kind of spurious comparison. W5 fails as a &quot;pure&quot; Werewolf game. And its failings, in my opinion, go quite a ways beyond the kinds of changes you need to make to provide an entertaining Crossover game in pre-X5 editions. Trying to apply the same standards is unreasonable, as far as I'm concerned. I'm being upfront about the fact that this interpretation is not for Werewolf purists. Or (insert-gameline) purists of any kind. It's a Crossover, and aside from my personal preferences in taste, it's primary job is to make the necessary compromises. </div> </div> </div>Some of the changes do come up in crossover as concerns. The power level of always-available Crinos, access to the Penumbra, tribal takes on crossover that would make them less than cooperative due to an established history (Silent Striders would go well with Mummy, Wraith, or Orpheus, not so well with Vampire), and their duties before the spirits, as well as the Litany.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This really feels like a fundamental disagreement on taste. I don't accept that having the Apocalypse be imminent inevitably diminishes the dramatic value/tension that comes from the option to run. Think of Sam's speech at the end of the film version of The Two Towers. Having the end staring you in the face, and still choosing to press on, is an awesome mood, I think. </div> </div> </div>If you have a ring to ferry to Mt. Doom, sure. Recall that Sam and Frodo were doing what they did to short cut the war and score a &quot;Sauron's power is forever diminished below the level he would need to threaten Middle-Earth&quot; win.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think I'd need a bit more specific examples to say more about how I'd address the issues, but I do broadly agree that you can't just take the problems as presented in each individual game-line and try and force them to fit together. A fair amount of revision is necessary. But it's doable, and even enjoyable at times. </div> </div> </div>Did vampires turn humans against Garou, or did the Garou make it possible with the Impergium? Did mages exist because humans are naturally curious, or did Garou drive the humans to seek out that forbidden power because of the Impergium? Were the Mokole wrong for trying to turn primates into something more like the Kings over their long millennia of selective hunting, which makes some of them veiled to even Garou, because it was kind of like the Impergium that would later follow?<br /> <br /> Other games have scenarios where things happened like Hermetics being tightwads about their mystic secrets leading up to Mistridge, the fae using religion as a dirty bomb against each other until it caused the Shattering, and vampires just being cursed to begin with according to almost everyone, most of all themselves.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I mean, there is theoretically room for one more layer down, what would be called Prime in Mage: the absolute base level monism, the stuff that can be literally anything. What I'm discussing is the idea that said &quot;Universal Substance&quot; could express itself in different ways. I personally kind of prefer a dualism of Change/Stasis (Order/Chaos also works, but has a lot of other baggage attached I kind of like to avoid). But I'm not at all opposed to having the Triat representing the most basic functions of reality, either. It just has implications that need to be worked through.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Fair enough. Also, quick question: is &quot;Shenti&quot; a term that originated in Werewolf or Mage? It'd been a little while since I looked at the concept, and I initially assumed Werewolf, but the wiki kind of makes it sound like more of a Mage concept. (I know the wiki isn't great; I use it as a quick reference and a starting point for deeper research on a topic.) </div> </div> </div>Mage.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm not sure if we're even in disagreement here, aside from maybe some semantics? Or there's a lot more about the differences between Triat and Trinity that I am missing.<br /> <br /> I would essentially agree with what you've characterized here: To use one example, Stasis is the River, and the Weaver is the River-spirit. I am 100% in agreement that they are fundamentally intertwined and that something affecting one will have profound consequences on the other. If you kill the Weaver, you destroy Stasis, and Reality itself probably collapses in on itself in the process.<br /> <br /> But while they are inextricably bound together, I do feel like there's an extent to which you can speak about them as separate things. The Body and the Soul are tightly bound together, and anything you do to one part will impact the whole. But even as they are part of the same whole, they possess certain aspects and traits which are radically different from one another, and you can talk about those particular components separate from each other while still acknowledging that they are connected.<br /> <br /> The fact that the Gauntlet exists, and divides the spiritual and material parts of reality, suggests to me that there is some value in discussing them as distinct from each other, even if you think they are ultimately connected at the root. </div> </div> </div>No when the setting is animistic and the spiritual part is treated as more important. If you were to go and dam the river, its spirit would persist, for example. Blowing up the planet does not kill the Celestine that claims it, but it is a terrible blow to them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, I got around to checking W20 307, and I feel like the fact that it explicitly mentions the existence of the Tellurian as something which is supposed to be bigger than Gaia kind of supports the argument I'm going for. But I also feel like I might need to clarify something: I'm not rejecting the idea that Gaia's influence extends beyond the Material World and the Penumbra, into the Near Umbra and the various Realms contained within. I am including those within my concept of &quot;This World&quot; and I apologize if failing to make that clear has caused any communication issues.<br /> <br /> What I'm focused on is what's being hit on by the conflict between Werewolf and Mage theories of the universe. If you accept the Werewolf framing, that there is an infinite material universe entirely separate from the Deep Umbra, then you leave room for the idea that there is life out on those other worlds, and that Gaia is the Mother-Goddess of them as well. I'm rejecting that premise. </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pEZgJyTzqPg\" data-code=\"pEZgJyTzqPg\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/pEZgJyTzqPg/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> (I kid. Somewhat.)<br /> <br /> Though, with W:tA, it's more like there was life on those worlds. Now it could be like Dead Space. That'd send the VEs scurrying home as fast as they could manage.<br /> <br /> &quot;You're back already?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Planet's haunted.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;That's against regu!...&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Planet's. Haunted.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But I did recently run into another tidbit that forces me to acknowledge that I'm fighting against the current in Werewolf more than I initially realized; while reading about the planetary Incarna, I encountered the idea that Luna is supposed to be the spirit of ALL Moons, while Sohkta/Phoebe is just the Incarna of Earth's Moon. Which would also conflict with the concept I'm pitching.<br /> <br /> <br /> The title of this thread is &quot;Suggested setting changes to make crossover easier.&quot; That Crossover is desirable is built into the premise of the discussion. I'd love help finding and addressing the challenges that come up in Crossover. But simply arguing that Crossover is a bad idea in the first place seems kind of contrarian when the whole conversation is about wanting to play Crossover games. </div> </div> </div>Crossover is a pain in the ass, first and foremost, because the games have their own flavor, and a lot of times, players flock to a game because they don't like the themes and play style of one or more of the others. I don't fancy playing personal horror fests, so Vampire is something I don't really have any desire to play, ever. Crossover that injects more personal horror into other games would be similarly irritating to me (especially since this is how V5 and its interpretation of the WoD is going). Demon would be in a similar boat, with an extra helping of &quot;I don't want to play in a Christian Biblical literalist setting&quot;.<br /> <br /> With Mage, I tend to object more to utterly over the top genre clash it presents, and also don't really subscribe to the notion that &quot;all things are just magic with a Special K.&quot; A secret society has some rad killer cyborgs? Sure, we all love going up against rad killer cyborgs. Having access to antimatter reactor powered spaceship fleets, space prisons for the inhabitants of Hogwarts, and a fucking Dyson sphere? Too advanced for the modern milieu, stopped caring.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-11T11:44:18-08:00","id":1528379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1527695-suggested-setting-changes-to-make-crossover-easier?p=1528373#post1528373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The business with MIR wouldn't be possible in W:tA if space and the Umbra were one and the same, because it involved BSDs hiding out in the spiritual shadow of it while spooking the cosmonauts from time to time. With the rising trend of commerical spaceflight, Garou are also incredibly likely to either hitch rides or go to the Aetherial Realm and head, say, Musk's plans for Mars off at the pass by stepping sideways into the habitat modules and making sure that Mars stays very, very red.<br /> <br /> There's also a plot hook in the Revised W:tA Storyteller's Handbook involving aliens from space that have nothing to do with the Umbra, and I'm not willing to dispense with that as a potential plot seed. That's XCOM, baby!</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure MIR would be off the table, though I only have the vaguest recollection of that particular plot point. I feel like Mage definitely has some sense that physical &quot;space&quot; continues to exist at least as far as the Moon, which is how you get Darkside Moon Base *and* a lunar Penumbra *and* the Court of Sohkta all being up there at once.<br /> <br /> The point about physical-universe aliens being in Werewolf Revised was a point I was unfamiliar with, and I absolutely agree that you'd have to make sacrifices or put a fair bit of work into splitting the difference. I feel like I could make it work to my satisfaction, but it might not suit your tastes.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1527695-suggested-setting-changes-to-make-crossover-easier?p=1528373#post1528373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They were also (I suppose one could say unhelpfully) written that way entirely on purpose. Except when they weren't, like with Mummy 2nd edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not quite sure what you were getting at here. Please explain?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1527695-suggested-setting-changes-to-make-crossover-easier?p=1528373#post1528373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could do without any of Vampire's metaplot style, frankly. &quot;Watch while you're helpless to do anything, pathetic neonates!&quot; can go die.</div> </div> </div> </div>As I've said, I enjoy Cosmic Horror, so &quot;monsters so powerful that you are utterly helpless against them&quot; is a trope I enjoy, in moderation at least. But I'm not a fan of Antediluvians-as-divine or as keystones of reality, etc. They're just vampires, bigger and badder. And killing them is entirely on the table, in my books, though you need to bring some serious heat.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1527695-suggested-setting-changes-to-make-crossover-easier?p=1528373#post1528373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some games managed to weld it together better than others. KotE, while being saddled with a heavy orientalist bent, had a construction mashing together the Middle and Dark Umbrae that didn't manage to step on anyone's toes. Regrettably, it also had Blood and Silk, which decided that it needed to push the Hakken as the only Garou other than the Stargazers in the Beast Courts. And which were known by that name, all the way back during the earliest part of the Chinese history, a good two thousand years before it would have made any sense at all (two strikes for being Japanese in ancient China before the Yayoi had even finished their migration to Japan, and also because Buddhism didn't become a thing until several centuries BCE, the Virtues of which are what the Hakken were named for).</div> </div> </div> </div>Broadly in agreement about KoTE, both on it doing a decent job bringing things together and being a bit of an Orientalist mess. Trying to figure out what are the good parts to keep and what needs to be revised is another part of all this, haha. I'm of two minds about the August Personage of Jade, and the idea that the Ebon Dragon and Scarlet Phoenix are the two remaining Angels on Earth; I like the way it brings the world together a bit more, but it once again becomes a mess with how firmly the rest of Demon attaches itself to Christian myths.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1527695-suggested-setting-changes-to-make-crossover-easier?p=1528373#post1528373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some of the changes do come up in crossover as concerns. The power level of always-available Crinos, access to the Penumbra, tribal takes on crossover that would make them less than cooperative due to an established history (Silent Striders would go well with Mummy, Wraith, or Orpheus, not so well with Vampire), and their duties before the spirits, as well as the Litany.</div> </div> </div> </div>Power level concerns are absolutely a thing, but I see that as a problem to resolve with players, not something that needs to be fixed when putting together the setting. And I also agree that, even when you make the effort for a Crossover-friendly setting, you need to try and work around the various agendas and priorities that different types of characters will bring to the table. And depending on what kind of game you want to play, some options might be inappropriate.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1527695-suggested-setting-changes-to-make-crossover-easier?p=1528373#post1528373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you have a ring to ferry to Mt. Doom, sure. Recall that Sam and Frodo were doing what they did to short cut the war and score a &quot;Sauron's power is forever diminished below the level he would need to threaten Middle-Earth&quot; win.</div> </div> </div> </div>I realized as soon as I said it that the situation on Middle-Earth is a bit more of a &quot;nowhere to run&quot; setup. I still feel like the words and feelings from that speech get across what I'm talking about, though, even if I can admit that the analogy kind of failed.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1527695-suggested-setting-changes-to-make-crossover-easier?p=1528373#post1528373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did vampires turn humans against Garou, or did the Garou make it possible with the Impergium? Did mages exist because humans are naturally curious, or did Garou drive the humans to seek out that forbidden power because of the Impergium? Were the Mokole wrong for trying to turn primates into something more like the Kings over their long millennia of selective hunting, which makes some of them veiled to even Garou, because it was kind of like the Impergium that would later follow?<br /> <br /> Other games have scenarios where things happened like Hermetics being tightwads about their mystic secrets leading up to Mistridge, the fae using religion as a dirty bomb against each other until it caused the Shattering, and vampires just being cursed to begin with according to almost everyone, most of all themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>A lot of those questions won't have strictly binary answers, but I've got at least rough ideas for most of them:<br /> <br /> The Garou probably managed to turn humanity against them mostly on their own, though I imagine the Kindred were happy to help.<br /> <br /> The next two questions actually kind of roll together! Mages exist because the Mokole tried to recreate their Drachids and accidentally created something with spiritual/magical potential far beyond what they had anticipated. Seeing as how I actively embrace Nihilism/Existentialism, I don't really have an objective answer as to whether or not it was the &quot;wrong&quot; decision, but I feel like a lot of Garou and Fera would probably say yes.<br /> <br /> (The part about the Mokole creating a Veil that even affects the Garou is something I've never heard before, and I'd appreciate more details or a source to investigate <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />)<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1527695-suggested-setting-changes-to-make-crossover-easier?p=1528373#post1528373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you!<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1527695-suggested-setting-changes-to-make-crossover-easier?p=1528373#post1528373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No when the setting is animistic and the spiritual part is treated as more important. If you were to go and dam the river, its spirit would persist, for example. Blowing up the planet does not kill the Celestine that claims it, but it is a terrible blow to them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I still feel like the example holds? Not 100%; I think a Body is hypothetically capable of surviving without a Soul in WoD, but would probably wind up dead pretty quick without someone taking care of it. Meanwhile, the Soul is *attached* to Material Reality by its body, but destroying the Body doesn't necessarily destroy the Soul. There is a sense that the spiritual part is more eternal, more capable of existing independently, even if they both depend on each other to a significant extent.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1527695-suggested-setting-changes-to-make-crossover-easier?p=1528373#post1528373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pEZgJyTzqPg\" data-code=\"pEZgJyTzqPg\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/pEZgJyTzqPg/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> (I kid. Somewhat.)</div> </div> </div> </div>And I can appreciate a good TFS reference <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1527695-suggested-setting-changes-to-make-crossover-easier?p=1528373#post1528373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though, with W:tA, it's more like there was life on those worlds. Now it could be like Dead Space. That'd send the VEs scurrying home as fast as they could manage.<br /> <br /> &quot;You're back already?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Planet's haunted.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;That's against regu!...&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Planet's. Haunted.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>That's actually an example that makes me consider that it may be more fun to throw Mage's assumptions about cosmology out, lol. Or at least put more work into finding a middle-ground between it and Werewolf.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1527695-suggested-setting-changes-to-make-crossover-easier?p=1528373#post1528373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Crossover is a pain in the ass, first and foremost, because the games have their own flavor, and a lot of times, players flock to a game because they don't like the themes and play style of one or more of the others. I don't fancy playing personal horror fests, so Vampire is something I don't really have any desire to play, ever. Crossover that injects more personal horror into other games would be similarly irritating to me (especially since this is how V5 and its interpretation of the WoD is going). Demon would be in a similar boat, with an extra helping of &quot;I don't want to play in a Christian Biblical literalist setting&quot;.<br /> <br /> With Mage, I tend to object more to utterly over the top genre clash it presents, and also don't really subscribe to the notion that &quot;all things are just magic with a Special K.&quot; A secret society has some rad killer cyborgs? Sure, we all love going up against rad killer cyborgs. Having access to antimatter reactor powered spaceship fleets, space prisons for the inhabitants of Hogwarts, and a fucking Dyson sphere? Too advanced for the modern milieu, stopped caring.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't worry, I will never invite you to play any Crossover games with me!<br /> <br /> Once again, I agree that these ideas are not good for people who are very interested in the themes of one particular game, and less interested in the others. This is for the folks who want something different.<br /> <br /> I definitely agree that I'm not big on the Biblical literalism of Demon. As I've noted, it remains one of the big sticking points in my Theory of Everything, haha.<br /> <br /> I also get the concerns with Mage. I really like a lot of stuff about Mage, but a lot of the stuff with the Technocracy starts to get a bit wonky because they have to be Mages as well. I feel like giving them rules that forced them to stick a bit closer to harder sci-fi might have benefited them: I just don't think I'll ever be 100% OK with a Syndic bankrupting someone so hard that they are wiped out of existence entirely. And yeah, you have to tone down just how powerful the Technocracy is in order to make it fit into a Crossover reasonably well. But I feel like taking into account the influence that all the other Splats would have had on the world helps justify doing so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-11T15:13:43-08:00","id":1528399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1527695-suggested-setting-changes-to-make-crossover-easier?p=1528379#post1528379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not sure MIR would be off the table, though I only have the vaguest recollection of that particular plot point. I feel like Mage definitely has some sense that physical &quot;space&quot; continues to exist at least as far as the Moon, which is how you get Darkside Moon Base *and* a lunar Penumbra *and* the Court of Sohkta all being up there at once.<br /> <br /> The point about physical-universe aliens being in Werewolf Revised was a point I was unfamiliar with, and I absolutely agree that you'd have to make sacrifices or put a fair bit of work into splitting the difference. I feel like I could make it work to my satisfaction, but it might not suit your tastes.</div> </div> </div> </div>A few of Mage's other approaches to the Umbra also don't sit well with other games, like saying that a vidare of death means that stepping sideways makes you view all the Umbra as the Underworld. Those are established places in the spirit world that you don't just get to.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm not quite sure what you were getting at here. Please explain? </div> </div> </div>Sometimes the people who were making the game were more open to crossover than others. Mummy 2nd edition, as a written, is a mass crossover romp in the making to restore the Osirian League (Bubasti Bastet, the Mokole-mbembe, Silent Strider Garou, Children of Osiris vampires/hunters, Hem ka Sobek Mages and a few others alongside the Shemsu Heru) versus primarily the Followers of Set, bane mummies, and some more direct servants of Apep. That was the ideal floated; it was kind of like the Garou and Fera situation, but across several game lines. And for those particular splats of those particular games, having a rumble in Egypt made sense, kind of like the better parts of KotE. It often seems like digging into a shared cultural background tends to improve things, like with the Beast Courts not being out to utterly exterminate every one of the Hungry Dead (though in their defense, the Hungry Dead don't increase their numbers anywhere nearly as quickly as Kindred do with their punctuated mass embrace events).<br /> <br /> I doubt that you'd get Silver Fangs being friendly with the Ventrue, though. That relationship probably mirrors the Shadow Lords vs. the Tzimisce. The Sidhe, however, can glue together the Silver Fangs and Fianna! Trolls can have a good time killing vargr with the Fenrir! Honestly, a lot of this seems to hinge successful crossover on &quot;which vampires have pissed us off, and how many more do you want to bet you can kill than us?&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As I've said, I enjoy Cosmic Horror, so &quot;monsters so powerful that you are utterly helpless against them&quot; is a trope I enjoy, in moderation at least. But I'm not a fan of Antediluvians-as-divine or as keystones of reality, etc. They're just vampires, bigger and badder. And killing them is entirely on the table, in my books, though you need to bring some serious heat. </div> </div> </div>That's one of the more contentious areas, especially with Incarna vs. Aeon vs. Antediluvian.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Broadly in agreement about KoTE, both on it doing a decent job bringing things together and being a bit of an Orientalist mess. Trying to figure out what are the good parts to keep and what needs to be revised is another part of all this, haha. I'm of two minds about the August Personage of Jade, and the idea that the Ebon Dragon and Scarlet Phoenix are the two remaining Angels on Earth; I like the way it brings the world together a bit more, but it once again becomes a mess with how firmly the rest of Demon attaches itself to Christian myths. </div> </div> </div>I could do with the &quot;angel&quot; designation being more of a personal filter for the speaker.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Power level concerns are absolutely a thing, but I see that as a problem to resolve with players, not something that needs to be fixed when putting together the setting. And I also agree that, even when you make the effort for a Crossover-friendly setting, you need to try and work around the various agendas and priorities that different types of characters will bring to the table. And depending on what kind of game you want to play, some options might be inappropriate. </div> </div> </div>Another issue with Werewolf is that its Splatter milieu means that characters just... aren't safe. Death can easily come to visit and bring along his trashy friends, Ludicrous Gibs and Horrible Maiming. And dialing back the violence means that maybe any bits of W:tA should sit the game out, because even a good day for W:tA tends to be a bit bloody by other games' standards. Death or glory doesn't always appeal.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I realized as soon as I said it that the situation on Middle-Earth is a bit more of a &quot;nowhere to run&quot; setup. I still feel like the words and feelings from that speech get across what I'm talking about, though, even if I can admit that the analogy kind of failed. </div> </div> </div>I suppose that Gandalf could have busted out some extra stuff, but the price...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A lot of those questions won't have strictly binary answers, but I've got at least rough ideas for most of them:<br /> <br /> The Garou probably managed to turn humanity against them mostly on their own, though I imagine the Kindred were happy to help.<br /> <br /> The next two questions actually kind of roll together! Mages exist because the Mokole tried to recreate their Drachids and accidentally created something with spiritual/magical potential far beyond what they had anticipated. Seeing as how I actively embrace Nihilism/Existentialism, I don't really have an objective answer as to whether or not it was the &quot;wrong&quot; decision, but I feel like a lot of Garou and Fera would probably say yes.<br /> <br /> (The part about the Mokole creating a Veil that even affects the Garou is something I've never heard before, and I'd appreciate more details or a source to investigate <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />) </div> </div> </div>Mokole Breedbook. It shows up in the history chapter and as the 7 point Merit, Veiled to Garou (though that should really be rephrased as &quot;Primeval Veil&quot; and work against every mammal changer).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I still feel like the example holds? Not 100%; I think a Body is hypothetically capable of surviving without a Soul in WoD, but would probably wind up dead pretty quick without someone taking care of it. Meanwhile, the Soul is *attached* to Material Reality by its body, but destroying the Body doesn't necessarily destroy the Soul. There is a sense that the spiritual part is more eternal, more capable of existing independently, even if they both depend on each other to a significant extent. </div> </div> </div>Spirits of the natural world are a bit different from living beings that are spiritually connected. They haven't yet joined in on the interconnected background existence yet, though some Garou and Fera painlessly step out of their bodies as ancestor-spirits.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And I can appreciate a good TFS reference <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> </div> </div> </div>&quot;I am hilarious, and you will quote everything I say!&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's actually an example that makes me consider that it may be more fun to throw Mage's assumptions about cosmology out, lol. Or at least put more work into finding a middle-ground between it and Werewolf. </div> </div> </div>I'm still not sure that could be done without making an entirely new game. You might need to roll Mage back to Dark Ages: Mage style Foundation and Pillars, which people seem to not like for being &quot;too rules heavy&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Don't worry, I will never invite you to play any Crossover games with me! </div> </div> </div>Well, that's a relief!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Once again, I agree that these ideas are not good for people who are very interested in the themes of one particular game, and less interested in the others. This is for the folks who want something different.<br /> <br /> I definitely agree that I'm not big on the Biblical literalism of Demon. As I've noted, it remains one of the big sticking points in my Theory of Everything, haha.<br /> <br /> I also get the concerns with Mage. I really like a lot of stuff about Mage, but a lot of the stuff with the Technocracy starts to get a bit wonky because they have to be Mages as well. I feel like giving them rules that forced them to stick a bit closer to harder sci-fi might have benefited them: I just don't think I'll ever be 100% OK with a Syndic bankrupting someone so hard that they are wiped out of existence entirely. And yeah, you have to tone down just how powerful the Technocracy is in order to make it fit into a Crossover reasonably well. But I feel like taking into account the influence that all the other Splats would have had on the world helps justify doing so. </div> </div> </div>Well, one method of toning down the Technocracy is to have the Weaver-spirits behind Shinzui and OneSong eat it alive while SPD introduces another large contingent to their &quot;dear friends and colleagues&quot;. It'd be like the Lotus Massacre from Return of the Scarlet Empress, but with more corruption and assimilation. It's also the logical end point of the systems that the Technos set up - having made something so &quot;perfect&quot;, they are inevitably consumed by it in turn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-11T22:28:32-08:00","id":1528407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1527695-suggested-setting-changes-to-make-crossover-easier?p=1528399#post1528399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A few of Mage's other approaches to the Umbra also don't sit well with other games, like saying that a vidare of death means that stepping sideways makes you view all the Umbra as the Underworld. Those are established places in the spirit world that you don't just get to.</div> </div> </div> </div>Vidare are just kind of weird, agreed. Given that the different Penumbras actually do exist, it's weird to also have a set of strange perspective-filters that seem to correlate with those Penumbras, but aren't them and actually bleed over into the other ones. I'm not sure if I'd leave the Vidare stuff as-is even in a pure Mage game. I'm OK with everyone having a somewhat-unique perception of their surroundings in the Umbra, but the Vidare come across a little too strong.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1527695-suggested-setting-changes-to-make-crossover-easier?p=1528399#post1528399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sometimes the people who were making the game were more open to crossover than others. Mummy 2nd edition, as a written, is a mass crossover romp in the making to restore the Osirian League (Bubasti Bastet, the Mokole-mbembe, Silent Strider Garou, Children of Osiris vampires/hunters, Hem ka Sobek Mages and a few others alongside the Shemsu Heru) versus primarily the Followers of Set, bane mummies, and some more direct servants of Apep. That was the ideal floated; it was kind of like the Garou and Fera situation, but across several game lines. And for those particular splats of those particular games, having a rumble in Egypt made sense, kind of like the better parts of KotE. It often seems like digging into a shared cultural background tends to improve things, like with the Beast Courts not being out to utterly exterminate every one of the Hungry Dead (though in their defense, the Hungry Dead don't increase their numbers anywhere nearly as quickly as Kindred do with their punctuated mass embrace events).<br /> <br /> I doubt that you'd get Silver Fangs being friendly with the Ventrue, though. That relationship probably mirrors the Shadow Lords vs. the Tzimisce. The Sidhe, however, can glue together the Silver Fangs and Fianna! Trolls can have a good time killing vargr with the Fenrir! Honestly, a lot of this seems to hinge successful crossover on &quot;which vampires have pissed us off, and how many more do you want to bet you can kill than us?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought that might be what you were getting at, but I wasn't certain. I've generally assumed it's more &quot;some creators liked Crossover, some didn't&quot; rather than a matter of timing. Despite a lot of people pointing out that Revised is where we get some of the firmest anti-Crossover positions, it's also the time of the Week of Nightmares and Blood Treachery. It just feels like an argument among the game designers that could never get fully settled. And people are still fighting about it 20 years later, haha.<br /> <br /> I feel like there are Watsonian and Doylist arguments for how the &quot;shared culture&quot; situation tended to help smooth Crossover. From the Watsonian perspective, having the different Splats talking to each other means they're going to know more about each other's beliefs, and whatever shared ideas they have about their various origins will have encountered the points of conflict and probably had to come to some kind of resolution around them. From the Doylist perspective, they have less excuse for things not to mesh when Crossover is a core part of the product.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1527695-suggested-setting-changes-to-make-crossover-easier?p=1528399#post1528399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's one of the more contentious areas, especially with Incarna vs. Aeon vs. Antediluvian.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not going to say I don't ponder those questions, but I don't spend too much time on them. I feel like once I've decided on what the underlying metaphysics are, the answers to those questions will become self-evident. But broadly, I feel like the Antediluvians are probably at the lower end of the Big Fish power-scale, in my reckoning. Closer to Archmages than Incarna. Probably. Again, haven't spent too much time on this issue, so I've only got a vague idea on the power levels of the &quot;statless&quot;-level spirits.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1527695-suggested-setting-changes-to-make-crossover-easier?p=1528399#post1528399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could do with the &quot;angel&quot; designation being more of a personal filter for the speaker.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed, but IIRC the speaker in question was Lucifer Morningstar, so that complicates things.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1527695-suggested-setting-changes-to-make-crossover-easier?p=1528399#post1528399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another issue with Werewolf is that its Splatter milieu means that characters just... aren't safe. Death can easily come to visit and bring along his trashy friends, Ludicrous Gibs and Horrible Maiming. And dialing back the violence means that maybe any bits of W:tA should sit the game out, because even a good day for W:tA tends to be a bit bloody by other games' standards. Death or glory doesn't always appeal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep. Also, I'm personally a fan of taking the option offered by M20 and letting combat with spirits and such remain every bit as nasty as it is in W20, knowing full well that it makes spirits way more dangerous to Mages. I'm Mage-centric in the sense that I love the postmodernism of Consensual Reality, but I am very happy to put the little punks in their place as well.<br /> <br /> Arguing that Garou should be able to exist in the same universe as other Splats is definitely not the same thing as suggesting they should all go ass-kicking together. Not unless the members of the other Splats coming along for the ride are combat-optimized enough not to be in (more) danger of ending up bloody pudding. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1527695-suggested-setting-changes-to-make-crossover-easier?p=1528399#post1528399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mokole Breedbook. It shows up in the history chapter and as the 7 point Merit, Veiled to Garou (though that should really be rephrased as &quot;Primeval Veil&quot; and work against every mammal changer).</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks again! I've never actually tracked down the original source on the idea that the Mokole were behind human evolution. I'm guessing that's in there as well? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1527695-suggested-setting-changes-to-make-crossover-easier?p=1528399#post1528399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Spirits of the natural world are a bit different from living beings that are spiritually connected. They haven't yet joined in on the interconnected background existence yet, though some Garou and Fera painlessly step out of their bodies as ancestor-spirits.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mhm, I was using it as an analogy, I understand it's not an identical case.<br /> <br /> To try and get back to the point I'm asking about, a River can exist on one side of the Gauntlet, while the River-Spirit is on the other side of the Gauntlet, and presumably can move around, go other places, do other things, perhaps even communicate if its something more powerful and complex like a Jaggling. If they are One Thing, that One Thing is capable of existing in more than one place, expressing certain characteristics in one aspect which are not present in the other aspect. So to return to my original question, why can't there be an analogous relationship between the Metaphysical Trinity (the River) and the Triat (the River-spirit)? Are there aspects of one which fundamentally contradict the other and make the idea of a connection between them unworkable?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1527695-suggested-setting-changes-to-make-crossover-easier?p=1528399#post1528399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;I am hilarious, and you will quote everything I say!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;... God damn it, Nappa...&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1527695-suggested-setting-changes-to-make-crossover-easier?p=1528399#post1528399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm still not sure that could be done without making an entirely new game. You might need to roll Mage back to Dark Ages: Mage style Foundation and Pillars, which people seem to not like for being &quot;too rules heavy&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm talking very specifically about the contradiction in how Outer Space is supposed to work, not a general Mage/Werewolf hybrid that is meant to perfectly balance the two. I do know that no Crossover game can give all game-lines their full due, but I genuinely try my best to give them all a fair shake. So while just defaulting to the Mage option seems easier, since I feel they spent more time on outer-space shenanigans and therefore would have more material you need to retcon if you didn't accept it as canon, I'm open to giving the Werewolf interpretation a bit of time as well.<br /> <br /> Actually, though, while pondering a lot of this stuff, and looking at stuff like Darkside, the Cop, and the Shard Realms again, I realized something. Mage's cosmology may not push out Werewolf's quite as bad as it seems, at least regarding the wider universe. I realized that some of the planets in our solar system are, by Mage standards, out in the Deep Umbra. Yet they maintain enough consistency in location and behaviour that, whatever other wonky magic rules are going on out there where normal folks can't see what's going on, they can be consistently mapped to particular locations. And then I started thinking about the Cop, how it's supposed to be out in Alpha Centauri. Whether you call it Outer Space or the Deep Umbra, it kind of seems like everything we expect to be out there in the physical universe remains out there even in Mage's Deep Umbra version. It just happens to be that the Gauntlet is non-existent, everywhere, all the time. Which, depending on your view of the source of the Gauntlet, might make perfect sense; I think even Werewolf puts forward the idea that deep dark abysses are another place where you tend to find a thin Gauntlet, and that's a pretty good descriptor for the cosmic void.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1527695-suggested-setting-changes-to-make-crossover-easier?p=1528399#post1528399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, one method of toning down the Technocracy is to have the Weaver-spirits behind Shinzui and OneSong eat it alive while SPD introduces another large contingent to their &quot;dear friends and colleagues&quot;. It'd be like the Lotus Massacre from Return of the Scarlet Empress, but with more corruption and assimilation. It's also the logical end point of the systems that the Technos set up - having made something so &quot;perfect&quot;, they are inevitably consumed by it in turn.</div> </div> </div> </div>I had to do a web-search to realize you were referring to Exalted. I know next to nothing about it, beyond brief wiki reads when it gets referred to in WoD threads, lol. So I'm afraid the scenario you're describing is going over my head a bit, though I get the gist.<br /> <br /> The Technocracy as Weaver-pawns would obviously be my go-to if I was running a Werewolf-centric game, for certain. And even my Crossover version gets to be a catspaw a lot of the time. But I've seen arguments put forward here on the forums that even the Technocrats are too Dynamic for the Weaver's taste, so I'm not sure if that's the route I want to go. I'm also wondering whether or not that's the road I want to go down with Control and Threat Null; the fact that the Autopolitans are explicitly described as serving the Computer suggests at least one group is under the influence of the Weaver, but that doesn't necessarily mean all of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-12T19:27:47-08:00","id":1528469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1527695-suggested-setting-changes-to-make-crossover-easier?p=1528407#post1528407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I thought that might be what you were getting at, but I wasn't certain. I've generally assumed it's more &quot;some creators liked Crossover, some didn't&quot; rather than a matter of timing. Despite a lot of people pointing out that Revised is where we get some of the firmest anti-Crossover positions, it's also the time of the Week of Nightmares and Blood Treachery.</div> </div> </div> </div>One could argue that those are attempts to make crossover look and handle as onerous as possible.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It just feels like an argument among the game designers that could never get fully settled. And people are still fighting about it 20 years later, haha. </div> </div> </div>The internet shall be won!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I feel like there are Watsonian and Doylist arguments for how the &quot;shared culture&quot; situation tended to help smooth Crossover. From the Watsonian perspective, having the different Splats talking to each other means they're going to know more about each other's beliefs, and whatever shared ideas they have about their various origins will have encountered the points of conflict and probably had to come to some kind of resolution around them. From the Doylist perspective, they have less excuse for things not to mesh when Crossover is a core part of the product. </div> </div> </div>Blood-Dimmed Tides was kind of a neutral version of that. Underwater is kind of a unique environment where everyone under the sea really does tend to have more in common with each other than with others one the surface.<br /> <br /> Except for the Gangrel Aquarii and their attempts to flat-out eat Rorqual. And no one likes the Chulorviah.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm not going to say I don't ponder those questions, but I don't spend too much time on them. I feel like once I've decided on what the underlying metaphysics are, the answers to those questions will become self-evident. But broadly, I feel like the Antediluvians are probably at the lower end of the Big Fish power-scale, in my reckoning. Closer to Archmages than Incarna. Probably. Again, haven't spent too much time on this issue, so I've only got a vague idea on the power levels of the &quot;statless&quot;-level spirits. </div> </div> </div>I've spent a bit longer on it, because someone actually made a post about vampire elders being better able to take on Maeljin than Garou. That was... a special thread.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Agreed, but IIRC the speaker in question was Lucifer Morningstar, so that complicates things. </div> </div> </div>Maybe even he isn't who or what he thinks he is. (^VVVVVVV^)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yep. Also, I'm personally a fan of taking the option offered by M20 and letting combat with spirits and such remain every bit as nasty as it is in W20, knowing full well that it makes spirits way more dangerous to Mages. I'm Mage-centric in the sense that I love the postmodernism of Consensual Reality, but I am very happy to put the little punks in their place as well.<br /> <br /> Arguing that Garou should be able to exist in the same universe as other Splats is definitely not the same thing as suggesting they should all go ass-kicking together. Not unless the members of the other Splats coming along for the ride are combat-optimized enough not to be in (more) danger of ending up bloody pudding. </div> </div> </div>I'm fond of likening it to Sam Peckinpah's Salad Days, myself.<br /> <br /> &quot;I say, Lionel, catch!&quot;<br /> <br /> [quote]<br /> Thanks again! I've never actually tracked down the original source on the idea that the Mokole were behind human evolution. I'm guessing that's in there as well? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Yeah. When you're hanging around for 65 million years, you have plenty of time to alter primate evolution, maybe.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Mhm, I was using it as an analogy, I understand it's not an identical case.<br /> <br /> To try and get back to the point I'm asking about, a River can exist on one side of the Gauntlet, while the River-Spirit is on the other side of the Gauntlet, and presumably can move around, go other places, do other things, perhaps even communicate if its something more powerful and complex like a Jaggling. If they are One Thing, that One Thing is capable of existing in more than one place, expressing certain characteristics in one aspect which are not present in the other aspect. So to return to my original question, why can't there be an analogous relationship between the Metaphysical Trinity (the River) and the Triat (the River-spirit)? Are there aspects of one which fundamentally contradict the other and make the idea of a connection between them unworkable? </div> </div> </div>Ah, I see where the confusion is. Yeah, I was mostly talking about how the spirit is the existence of the thing even if it is arguably independent. At that scale of reality, though, you'd be hard-pressed to destroy Stasis, Dynamism, or Entropy - but even if you did, the respective member of the Triat would just recreate it. Killing a member of the Triat? The related concept goes with it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm talking very specifically about the contradiction in how Outer Space is supposed to work, not a general Mage/Werewolf hybrid that is meant to perfectly balance the two. I do know that no Crossover game can give all game-lines their full due, but I genuinely try my best to give them all a fair shake. So while just defaulting to the Mage option seems easier, since I feel they spent more time on outer-space shenanigans and therefore would have more material you need to retcon if you didn't accept it as canon, I'm open to giving the Werewolf interpretation a bit of time as well.<br /> <br /> Actually, though, while pondering a lot of this stuff, and looking at stuff like Darkside, the Cop, and the Shard Realms again, I realized something. Mage's cosmology may not push out Werewolf's quite as bad as it seems, at least regarding the wider universe. I realized that some of the planets in our solar system are, by Mage standards, out in the Deep Umbra. Yet they maintain enough consistency in location and behaviour that, whatever other wonky magic rules are going on out there where normal folks can't see what's going on, they can be consistently mapped to particular locations. And then I started thinking about the Cop, how it's supposed to be out in Alpha Centauri. Whether you call it Outer Space or the Deep Umbra, it kind of seems like everything we expect to be out there in the physical universe remains out there even in Mage's Deep Umbra version. It just happens to be that the Gauntlet is non-existent, everywhere, all the time. Which, depending on your view of the source of the Gauntlet, might make perfect sense; I think even Werewolf puts forward the idea that deep dark abysses are another place where you tend to find a thin Gauntlet, and that's a pretty good descriptor for the cosmic void. </div> </div> </div>I still like there being a universal Gauntlet because of how pervasive the Weaver is in the universe, being a third of it (and completely confounded about the full breadth of understanding it!).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I had to do a web-search to realize you were referring to Exalted. I know next to nothing about it, beyond brief wiki reads when it gets referred to in WoD threads, lol. So I'm afraid the scenario you're describing is going over my head a bit, though I get the gist. </div> </div> </div>It was mostly because how Sidereals were the Exalted linked to Mages (in an Elseworlds re-imagining fashion), and the Bronze Faction is kind of like the Technocracy of its story in terms of social control.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Technocracy as Weaver-pawns would obviously be my go-to if I was running a Werewolf-centric game, for certain. And even my Crossover version gets to be a catspaw a lot of the time. But I've seen arguments put forward here on the forums that even the Technocrats are too Dynamic for the Weaver's taste, so I'm not sure if that's the route I want to go. I'm also wondering whether or not that's the road I want to go down with Control and Threat Null; the fact that the Autopolitans are explicitly described as serving the Computer suggests at least one group is under the influence of the Weaver, but that doesn't necessarily mean all of them. </div> </div> </div>In this case, it would more be a Triatic faction opening up in the TU, and then growing to be a tremendous problem as it assimilates more members of the Union into itself. Especially if a member of the Syndicate just learned about this hot new company that's going to work where they went wrong with Pentex and SPD (Shinzui). It's 100% clean from Entropic resonance, and there is no way that this could possibly go wrong!<br /> <br /> Smash cut to Drone-d Amalgalm members hunting down their fellows while the Syndicate op wonders where the hell things went wrong...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-13T12:40:29-08:00","id":1528493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1527695-suggested-setting-changes-to-make-crossover-easier?p=1528469#post1528469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One could argue that those are attempts to make crossover look and handle as onerous as possible.</div> </div> </div> </div>Blood Treachery was definitely punishing in regards to Ghoul Mages. But it does again explicitly bring the two actual Splats into the same room together, not the lore-neutral antagonist-versions you get in the core game-lines.<br /> <br /> I honestly love the over-the-top edge-lord silliness of the Week of Nightmares, which is part of why I'm such a Crossover fanboy. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1527695-suggested-setting-changes-to-make-crossover-easier?p=1528469#post1528469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The internet shall be won!</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say 'over my dead body,' but that may not even be the end! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1527695-suggested-setting-changes-to-make-crossover-easier?p=1528469#post1528469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Blood-Dimmed Tides was kind of a neutral version of that. Underwater is kind of a unique environment where everyone under the sea really does tend to have more in common with each other than with others one the surface.<br /> <br /> Except for the Gangrel Aquarii and their attempts to flat-out eat Rorqual. And no one likes the Chulorviah.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bad, wicked, naughty Gangrel Aquarii!<br /> <br /> Maybe I need to give Blood-Dimmed Tides another read, but the Chulorviah struck me as a bit of a stranded concept. The vibe I got was that Chulorviosis was Wyrmish or Wyrm-adjacent, but the Chulorviah were not really Wyrm servants. So Pentex being so on board with helping spread the infection seems a bit weird. If they genuinely just like throwing any and all kinds of shit around, sure, but it does seem like the leadership has specific plans and goals, not just chaos for its own sake, and the Chulorviah getting out of hand seems like the sort of thing that could actually interfere with their own schemes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1527695-suggested-setting-changes-to-make-crossover-easier?p=1528469#post1528469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've spent a bit longer on it, because someone actually made a post about vampire elders being better able to take on Maeljin than Garou. That was... a special thread.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, there are some edge-cases and semantics that might be worth some discussion. But broadly, oof.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1527695-suggested-setting-changes-to-make-crossover-easier?p=1528469#post1528469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe even he isn't who or what he thinks he is. (^VVVVVVV^)</div> </div> </div> </div>Totally an option, but you're throwing Demon under the bus pretty hard at that point. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1527695-suggested-setting-changes-to-make-crossover-easier?p=1528469#post1528469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm fond of likening it to Sam Peckinpah's Salad Days, myself.<br /> <br /> &quot;I say, Lionel, catch!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Went right over my head again, I'm afraid, but in this context I feel that may be a good thing <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1527695-suggested-setting-changes-to-make-crossover-easier?p=1528469#post1528469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah. When you're hanging around for 65 million years, you have plenty of time to alter primate evolution, maybe.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a neat idea, need to take the time to look at the source material to get the full context and decide how on board I really am.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1527695-suggested-setting-changes-to-make-crossover-easier?p=1528469#post1528469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, I see where the confusion is. Yeah, I was mostly talking about how the spirit is the existence of the thing even if it is arguably independent. At that scale of reality, though, you'd be hard-pressed to destroy Stasis, Dynamism, or Entropy - but even if you did, the respective member of the Triat would just recreate it. Killing a member of the Triat? The related concept goes with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah, I'm focusing on the metaphysical principles at play, not the viability for a N/PC to actually pull something like that off. You're playing on the scale of Voormas' endgame, at a minimum.<br /> <br /> On the idea of actually destroying a member of the Triat, I wonder if there might be room for one of their Incarna &quot;children&quot; to take over. The transition would certainly shake up the entirety of existence, but do you think that would leave room for the Universe to at least survive losing a member of the Triat like that? I feel like that idea may have been posited in the Apocalypse book, but I'm just pulling from fuzzy memories at the moment.<br /> <br /> I do think I favour a more balanced approach that treats the material and spiritual elements as dependent upon each other, but I'm not arguing that it's Werewolf canon or anything. I think it may be a carry-over from starting more in NWoD/CoD and being influenced by Forsaken. But that's even more a case of hazy recollection.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1527695-suggested-setting-changes-to-make-crossover-easier?p=1528469#post1528469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still like there being a universal Gauntlet because of how pervasive the Weaver is in the universe, being a third of it (and completely confounded about the full breadth of understanding it!).</div> </div> </div> </div>Reasonable enough! I could see room for a compromise where there are more places out there with a split between material and spirit than Mage postulates. Great opportunity for that Dead Space scenario you pitched <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1527695-suggested-setting-changes-to-make-crossover-easier?p=1528469#post1528469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It was mostly because how Sidereals were the Exalted linked to Mages (in an Elseworlds re-imagining fashion), and the Bronze Faction is kind of like the Technocracy of its story in terms of social control.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mhm, I'm familiar with the broad strokes, but I don't know any of the specifics.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1527695-suggested-setting-changes-to-make-crossover-easier?p=1528469#post1528469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In this case, it would more be a Triatic faction opening up in the TU, and then growing to be a tremendous problem as it assimilates more members of the Union into itself. Especially if a member of the Syndicate just learned about this hot new company that's going to work where they went wrong with Pentex and SPD (Shinzui). It's 100% clean from Entropic resonance, and there is no way that this could possibly go wrong!<br /> <br /> Smash cut to Drone-d Amalgalm members hunting down their fellows while the Syndicate op wonders where the hell things went wrong...</div> </div> </div> </div>If you wanted to break the Technocracy, that absolutely does sound like one really fun way to do it! Not an idea to use for every game, but one I will happily put on the shelf to pull down as needed, with your permission <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-13T20:17:14-08:00","id":1528519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1527695-suggested-setting-changes-to-make-crossover-easier?p=1528493#post1528493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Blood Treachery was definitely punishing in regards to Ghoul Mages. But it does again explicitly bring the two actual Splats into the same room together, not the lore-neutral antagonist-versions you get in the core game-lines.<br /> <br /> I honestly love the over-the-top edge-lord silliness of the Week of Nightmares, which is part of why I'm such a Crossover fanboy.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're nice in theory, but they never have Garou or Fera really deploy the big guns. It all turns into a Vampire or Technocracy show.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'd say 'over my dead body,' but that may not even be the end! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> </div> </div> </div>DEATH IS ONLY THE BEGINN... wait, that's Kult, shit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Bad, wicked, naughty Gangrel Aquarii!<br /> <br /> Maybe I need to give Blood-Dimmed Tides another read, but the Chulorviah struck me as a bit of a stranded concept. The vibe I got was that Chulorviosis was Wyrmish or Wyrm-adjacent, but the Chulorviah were not really Wyrm servants. So Pentex being so on board with helping spread the infection seems a bit weird. If they genuinely just like throwing any and all kinds of shit around, sure, but it does seem like the leadership has specific plans and goals, not just chaos for its own sake, and the Chulorviah getting out of hand seems like the sort of thing that could actually interfere with their own schemes. </div> </div> </div>Pretty much, but no other game was willing to take them in, so they drifted into the W20 Book of the Wyrm to stay. Would have made a great threat to have in light of worldwide sea level rise, but the fucking geniuses at PDX said &quot;no, street level action, no Umbra&quot;...<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> Totally an option, but you're throwing Demon under the bus pretty hard at that point. </div> </div> </div>I'm willing to throw Demon under some very, very large buses.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Went right over my head again, I'm afraid, but in this context I feel that may be a good thing <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> </div> </div> </div>It's an hilariously over the top parody of Sam Peckinpah's violent filmography, where the setting is just an upper class British picnic, but everyone's slightest action results in horrible, mortal injury with gallons of fake blood.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's a neat idea, need to take the time to look at the source material to get the full context and decide how on board I really am. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it's one of the brain-twisters, alongside &quot;Qyrl made Cthulhu but had to agree to shrink him or else be imprisoned in Sea, and that's where the Merdhuacha come from!&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Oh yeah, I'm focusing on the metaphysical principles at play, not the viability for a N/PC to actually pull something like that off. You're playing on the scale of Voormas' endgame, at a minimum.<br /> <br /> On the idea of actually destroying a member of the Triat, I wonder if there might be room for one of their Incarna &quot;children&quot; to take over. The transition would certainly shake up the entirety of existence, but do you think that would leave room for the Universe to at least survive losing a member of the Triat like that? I feel like that idea may have been posited in the Apocalypse book, but I'm just pulling from fuzzy memories at the moment. </div> </div> </div>This is literally the purpose of Ananasa with regard to the Weaver, though I think that in her totality, she may be a bit bigger than an Incarna. The Wyld is a bit too indistinct to have a meaningful separation in this regard, though, and the Wyrm is literally in a bunch of pieces all running in different directions, so that constitutes just about the only clear line of succession for the Triat.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I do think I favour a more balanced approach that treats the material and spiritual elements as dependent upon each other, but I'm not arguing that it's Werewolf canon or anything. I think it may be a carry-over from starting more in NWoD/CoD and being influenced by Forsaken. But that's even more a case of hazy recollection. </div> </div> </div>Perhaps.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Reasonable enough! I could see room for a compromise where there are more places out there with a split between material and spirit than Mage postulates. Great opportunity for that Dead Space scenario you pitched <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> </div> </div> </div>(Begins singing creepy version of Twinkle, Twinkle Little Star)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Mhm, I'm familiar with the broad strokes, but I don't know any of the specifics. </div> </div> </div>I won't go into it any more here. It easily gets into its own thing. Books full of its own thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you wanted to break the Technocracy, that absolutely does sound like one really fun way to do it! Not an idea to use for every game, but one I will happily put on the shelf to pull down as needed, with your permission <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> </div> </div> </div>I don't own that. Everything was a component of what was already in the books (particularly the Book of the Weaver), as filtered through the typical &quot;I have this great idea!&quot; member of the Syndicate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-14T02:26:03-08:00","id":1528528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1527695-suggested-setting-changes-to-make-crossover-easier?p=1528519#post1528519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm willing to throw Demon under some very, very large buses.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, you don't necesarily have to<br /> Demon<i> can work</i> in the previous frames of WoD<br /> Especially Vampire, tracing their curse back to the Archangels, Revelations of the Dark Mother deepdives in the whole Elohim-topic and previous/other universes<br /> Mage Ascension is basically what Luficer big plan with the Babel Project was/is<br /> Wraith and (by connection) Mummy is not really bothered the fact who and why actually built the Underworld - even the old editions, it was hinted or outright stated, the Underworld is not the &quot;true afterlife&quot; and you lands there when have some unfinihed business and/or something interferred the process and via Transcendece you probably could reach your final destination<br /> Hunter always had connections and powers from Above<br /> And strangely, even the Kindred of the East fits in, the Wan Xian were proto-hunters, and after a little detour in Yomi, the whole goal is to work your way in the Hundred Clouds, it is basically Wraith, just you have an undead body, working toward Transcendece; different route, same goal.<br /> The two that somewhat fit strangely is the Changleing and Werewolf, but neither really bothered by the &quot;Demon point of view&quot; so to speak<br /> The Dreaming (both near and far) - by it own accont - is a universe unto its own, a chimerical reality at the age of &quot;rational thinking&quot; an beyond.<br /> And the Umbra is the metaphysical spirit world, paring spirit with the material - and this not really contradicts the &quot;Demon point of view&quot; either how the Elohim created everything<br /> <br /> Houses of Fallen actually explains this, why there is a huge universe out there; they not conjured out of nothing planets and stars and so on!<br /> House of The Fundament created space so substance could exist, pushing back the Nothing of the Abyss and with the superdense &quot;pearl&quot; of infinite, matter itself, beginning with atoms and building from there, after that infinitely small and dense orb containing everything they would and could need exploded by a Big Bang, expanding, and filling up the space they made for the universe.<br /> From Hidrogen, via gravity and physical laws, stars formed exploded in to supernovas, magentars and Balck Holes kept everything in motion, denser, complicated materials apeared,and so on and so on, untill conditions and materials were present to form the planet with different minerals, water, and all<br /> So apeared matterial, physical laws, dimensions, concepts, ideals... and with them appeared their spirits, and the book actually mentions, the Elohim were aware of this &quot;byproduct&quot;, but not really bothered with it, because it not interfered their work and they not had anything to do with it<br /> (The funny thing is, - or biggest joke on a Demon character - the need to introduce the physical laws, dimensions, concepts and for the mto work, they had to intorduce entropy and time, so the process could start and continue, thus the eventual death of the universe was always planned - but it is not really a problem, becasue A, it is not the first attempt, as per Revelations of Dark Mother, and or B, Creation, as per Demon: the Fallen always just ment to be the &quot;first step&quot; so to speak, no matter what the Elohim belived about balance and infinity, the plan of the Second World, where not even the Seventh House had acces to (and most of the Elohim wasn't even awere) was always there and was always the end goal)<br /> <br /> It is not unlike the relationship with relegion and science. Evolution for example. At the moment evolution became in a sense a scientific religion; almost all scientists have accepted it and many are prepared to 'bend' their observations to fit in with it. Evolution as a universal and all-pervading process. Except when it is not, and we have species around that somehow forgot to either die out or evolve, despite the similar, the totally same conditions that kicked sometimes basically the same species to die out or take an evolutionary step forward. Sometimes backwards.<br /> Evolution most of the time, but not always, explains the &quot;how&quot; but not the 'why&quot;, or at least not gives a satisfactory answer and more often than not just falls apart, and have to be ignored, because most of the time, it is true.... but not always.<br /> This is not unlike the Newtonian laws, for example Newton's laws of motion work well for describing the motion of everyday objects at moderate speeds and scales. However, they break down when dealing with very small particles, such as atoms and subatomic particles, or when dealing with very high speeds, such as those approaching the speed of light. This not makes Newton's laws untrue or faulty, just while explains mutch, can't explaine everything. You need Einsteinian laws, but they again, sotps working at a point (around the point the universe false to be static) and you need Hawking's laws, but again while Newton, Einstein and Hawking are working perfectly and bases of several things... they can't explain the Why completely just the How<br /> <br /> The Werewolf, Material, Umbra all of them is the the <i>How</i><br /> The Elohim and their work is the <i>Why</i><br /> And the two are not contradicts or makes the other untrue!<br /> Creation, spirits, umbra, etc are just the stage, everything on it: the actors, the decorations, literally everything! The river and the spirit of the river, the material planes and spiritual worlds with tagging along paralel or overlaping universes and Qlippothic ones<br /> The Elohim and their work is the Why: the backstage, levers and pulleys and directors, run crew, stagehands, backstage crew, the professionals who work backstage during performances to keep the show running smoothly and safely and you ideally never could see and/or from the point of the audience, they not even exist<br /> And just like in Demon, the abscence of the backstage and the crew not necessarily means the Show on the stage can't go on (just without the supervision and support, eventually degrades)<br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","user":"Shadeprowler","date":". 01-14-2024, 06:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-14T03:06:16-08:00","id":1528530,"title":"","content":"GOD I hate this spam-flaging<br /> Lets try again, will delete the original<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1527695-suggested-setting-changes-to-make-crossover-easier?p=1528519#post1528519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm willing to throw Demon under some very, very large buses.<br /></div> </div> </div> </d