m were aware of this &quot;byproduct&quot;, but not really bothered with it, because it not interfered their work and they not had anything to do with it<br /> (The funny thing is, - or biggest joke on a Demon character - the need to introduce the physical laws, dimensions, concepts and for the mto work, they had to intorduce entropy and time, so the process could start and continue, thus the eventual death of the universe was always planned - but it is not really a problem, becasue A, it is not the first attempt, as per Revelations of Dark Mother, and or B, Creation, as per Demon: the Fallen always just ment to be the &quot;first step&quot; so to speak, no matter what the Elohim belived about balance and infinity, the plan of the Second World, where not even the Seventh House had acces to (and most of the Elohim wasn't even awere) was always there and was always the end goal)<br /> <br /> It is not unlike the relationship with relegion and science. Evolution for example. At the moment evolution became in a sense a scientific religion; almost all scientists have accepted it and many are prepared to 'bend' their observations to fit in with it. Evolution as a universal and all-pervading process. Except when it is not, and we have species around that somehow forgot to either die out or evolve, despite the similar, the totally same conditions that kicked sometimes basically the same species to die out or take an evolutionary step forward. Sometimes backwards.<br /> Evolution most of the time, but not always, explains the &quot;how&quot; but not the 'why&quot;, or at least not gives a satisfactory answer and more often than not just falls apart, and have to be ignored, because most of the time, it is true.... but not always.<br /> This is not unlike the Newtonian laws, for example Newton's laws of motion work well for describing the motion of everyday objects at moderate speeds and scales. However, they break down when dealing with very small particles, such as atoms and subatomic particles, or when dealing with very high speeds, such as those approaching the speed of light. This not makes Newton's laws untrue or faulty, just while explains mutch, can't explaine everything. You need Einsteinian laws, but they again, sotps working at a point (around the point the universe false to be static) and you need Hawking's laws, but again while Newton, Einstein and Hawking are working perfectly and bases of several things... they can't explain the Why completely just the How<br /> <br /> The Werewolf, Material, Umbra all of them is the the <i>How</i><br /> The Elohim and their work is the <i>Why</i><br /> And the two are not contradicts or makes the other untrue!<br /> Creation, spirits, umbra, etc are just the stage, everything on it: the actors, the decorations, literally everything! The river and the spirit of the river, the material planes and spiritual worlds with tagging along paralel or overlaping universes and Qlippothic ones<br /> The Elohim and their work is the Why: the backstage, levers and pulleys and directors, run crew, stagehands, backstage crew, the professionals who work backstage during performances to keep the show running smoothly and safely and you ideally never could see and/or from the point of the audience, they not even exist<br /> And just like in Demon, the abscence of the backstage and the crew not necessarily means the Show on the stage can't go on (just without the supervision and support, eventually degrades)</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem with all of this is that it still has the same fundamental problem of clashing themes that <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23\" data-vbnamecard=\"23\">Saur Ops Specialist</a> and I have been discussing. You can force the basic metaphysics to function, but there are general principles that don't mesh well. Everything about Mage being the ultimate goal of Project Babel and such places human beings in a special spot at the centre of importance in the cosmos. Werewolf postulates that humans are nothing more than a bunch of uppity apes causing problems. I'm not saying that I think the ideas are bad (that tends to be how I view the relationship between Mage and Demon, as well), but it does not jive with a cosmology that accepts the principles of Werewolf as foundational. And taking away that foundational aspect does cut into core themes of Werewolf. <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23\" data-vbnamecard=\"23\">Saur Ops Specialist</a> isn't throwing Demon under the bus because they <b>have</b> to. They are doing it because they <b>want</b> to. And it makes sense from their POV.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-14T11:26:38-08:00","id":1528553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1527695-suggested-setting-changes-to-make-crossover-easier?p=1528519#post1528519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're nice in theory, but they never have Garou or Fera really deploy the big guns. It all turns into a Vampire or Technocracy show.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see arguments that groups like the Garou have more incentive to keep their &quot;big guns&quot; in reserve, but I can definitely see where that would be disappointing. Never followed the &quot;Rage&quot; books too closely, so I don't know how much we get to enjoy the Garou Nation really &quot;going loud&quot; in those.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1527695-suggested-setting-changes-to-make-crossover-easier?p=1528519#post1528519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">DEATH IS ONLY THE BEGINN... wait, that's Kult, shit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or Brendan Fraser. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1527695-suggested-setting-changes-to-make-crossover-easier?p=1528519#post1528519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pretty much, but no other game was willing to take them in, so they drifted into the W20 Book of the Wyrm to stay. Would have made a great threat to have in light of worldwide sea level rise, but the fucking geniuses at PDX said &quot;no, street level action, no Umbra&quot;...</div> </div> </div> </div>*sad trombone*<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1527695-suggested-setting-changes-to-make-crossover-easier?p=1528519#post1528519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm willing to throw Demon under some very, very large buses.</div> </div> </div> </div>As noted, I feel like I understand where you're coming from, haha. Not quite there myself, yet, but I do feel like Demon may be one of the game-lines that gets treated pretty rough in order to jive with the rest without undercutting them too much.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1527695-suggested-setting-changes-to-make-crossover-easier?p=1528519#post1528519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's an hilariously over the top parody of Sam Peckinpah's violent filmography, where the setting is just an upper class British picnic, but everyone's slightest action results in horrible, mortal injury with gallons of fake blood.</div> </div> </div> </div>*web-search again* So like a Spaghetti Western, but as a Monty Python skit?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1527695-suggested-setting-changes-to-make-crossover-easier?p=1528519#post1528519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, it's one of the brain-twisters, alongside &quot;Qyrl made Cthulhu but had to agree to shrink him or else be imprisoned in Sea, and that's where the Merdhuacha come from!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Another reason to look at Blood-Dimmed Tides again?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1527695-suggested-setting-changes-to-make-crossover-easier?p=1528519#post1528519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is literally the purpose of Ananasa with regard to the Weaver, though I think that in her totality, she may be a bit bigger than an Incarna. The Wyld is a bit too indistinct to have a meaningful separation in this regard, though, and the Wyrm is literally in a bunch of pieces all running in different directions, so that constitutes just about the only clear line of succession for the Triat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ananasa was the example I had in mind. Fair point about the Wyld and Wyrm, though I did wonder if the various &quot;pieces&quot; of the Wyrm might be able to fulfill a similar function.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1527695-suggested-setting-changes-to-make-crossover-easier?p=1528519#post1528519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I won't go into it any more here. It easily gets into its own thing. Books full of its own thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's kind of why I haven't, hahaha. It sounds neat, but I've only got so much time, and like my urban fantasy/horror a little better.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1527695-suggested-setting-changes-to-make-crossover-easier?p=1528519#post1528519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't own that. Everything was a component of what was already in the books (particularly the Book of the Weaver), as filtered through the typical &quot;I have this great idea!&quot; member of the Syndicate.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Syndicate part is specifically what I'm referring, dunno if that's in the books. I'm vaguely familiar with the fact that a couple End Times scenarios have the Technocracy get assimilated like that. But I find the idea of the Syndicate trying to find an alternative to Pentex and stumbling into a *different* Triat-run megacorporation instead to be rather hilarious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-14T19:43:10-08:00","id":1528575,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25886\" data-vbnamecard=\"25886\">Kharnov</a> actually, the bit about Qyrl making Cthulhu and having to shrink him was in Rokea. I'm actually a bit averse to picking up or looking at it due to its author and his terrible history, but it's there.<br /> <br /> And now that I've covered that... (insert sickening neck cracking sounds from mood whiplash)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1527695-suggested-setting-changes-to-make-crossover-easier?p=1528530#post1528530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">GOD I hate this spam-flaging<br /> Lets try again, will delete the original<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> To be fair, you don't necesarily have to<br /> Demon<i> can work</i> in the previous frames of WoD<br /> Especially Vampire, tracing their curse back to the Archangels, Revelations of the Dark Mother deepdives in the whole Elohim-topic and previous/other universes<br /> Mage Ascension is basically what Luficer big plan with the Babel Project was/is<br /> Wraith and (by connection) Mummy is not really bothered the fact who and why actually built the Underworld - even the old editions, it was hinted or outright stated, the Underworld is not the &quot;true afterlife&quot; and you lands there when have some unfinihed business and/or something interferred the process and via Transcendece you probably could reach your final destination<br /> Hunter always had connections and powers from Above<br /> And strangely, even the Kindred of the East fits in, the Wan Xian were proto-hunters, and after a little detour in Yomi, the whole goal is to work your way in the Hundred Clouds, it is basically Wraith, just you have an undead body, working toward Transcendece; different route, same goal.<br /> The two that somewhat fit strangely is the Changleing and Werewolf, but neither really bothered by the &quot;Demon point of view&quot; so to speak<br /> The Dreaming (both near and far) - by it own accont - is a universe unto its own, a chimerical reality at the age of &quot;rational thinking&quot; an beyond.<br /> And the Umbra is the metaphysical spirit world, paring spirit with the material - and this not really contradicts the &quot;Demon point of view&quot; either how the Elohim created everything<br /> <br /> Houses of Fallen actually explains this, why there is a huge universe out there; they not conjured out of nothing planets and stars and so on!<br /> House of The Fundament created space so substance could exist, pushing back the Nothing of the Abyss and with the superdense &quot;pearl&quot; of infinite, matter itself, beginning with atoms and building from there, after that infinitely small and dense orb containing everything they would and could need exploded by a Big Bang, expanding, and filling up the space they made for the universe.<br /> From Hidrogen, via gravity and physical laws, stars formed exploded in to supernovas, while magnetars and Balck Holes kept everything in motion, denser, complicated materials apeared,and so on and so on, untill conditions and materials were present to form the desired planet with different minerals, water, and all<br /> So by this work apeared matterial, physical laws, dimensions, concepts, ideals... and with them appeared their spirits, and the book actually mentions, the Elohim were aware of this &quot;byproduct&quot;, but not really bothered with it, because it not interfered their work and they not had anything to do with it<br /> (The funny thing is, - or biggest joke on a Demon character - the need to introduce the physical laws, dimensions, concepts and for the mto work, they had to intorduce entropy and time, so the process could start and continue, thus the eventual death of the universe was always planned - but it is not really a problem, becasue A, it is not the first attempt, as per Revelations of Dark Mother, and or B, Creation, as per Demon: the Fallen always just ment to be the &quot;first step&quot; so to speak, no matter what the Elohim belived about balance and infinity, the plan of the Second World, where not even the Seventh House had acces to (and most of the Elohim wasn't even awere) was always there and was always the end goal)<br /> <br /> It is not unlike the relationship with relegion and science. Evolution for example. At the moment evolution became in a sense a scientific religion;</div> </div> </div> </div>NO<br /> <br /> FUCK THIS TIRED FUNDAMENTALIST TALKING POINT<br /> <br /> Acceptance of Evolution (Evolution with Developmental Biology or <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ydqReeTV_vk\" target=\"_blank\">Evo Devo</a> at this point) is because it's an exhaustive framework for understanding and explaining how life works and how it changes. There are no articles of faith and no blind leaps that you're being asked to take in learning it and how it applies to the world. Hundreds have brought the receipts to show how the world works here, and everyone can dip into this pool of Hard Facts to support use of it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> almost all scientists have accepted it and many are prepared to 'bend' their observations to fit in with it. Evolution as a universal and all-pervading process. Except when it is not, and we have species around that somehow forgot to either die out or evolve, despite the similar, the totally same conditions that kicked sometimes basically the same species to die out or take an evolutionary step forward. Sometimes backwards. </div> </div> </div>And here you're just bringing bullshit. Steaming loads of it. As long as organisms persist and have differential survival, their traits will have differential frequencies, which change, which is evolution. Read up on the Hardy-Weinberg Theorem to get an idea where evolution might actually slow down and don't @ me until you do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Evolution most of the time, but not always, explains the &quot;how&quot; but not the 'why&quot;, or at least not gives a satisfactory answer and more often than not just falls apart, and have to be ignored, because most of the time, it is true.... but not always. </div> </div> </div>Don't play god of the gaps with me. Hundreds more in the future will have refined the field even further. Don't hide your faith in those shadows, or it's going to end up getting lost.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is not unlike the Newtonian laws, for example Newton's laws of motion work well for describing the motion of everyday objects at moderate speeds and scales. However, they break down when dealing with very small particles, such as atoms and subatomic particles, or when dealing with very high speeds, such as those approaching the speed of light. This not makes Newton's laws untrue or faulty, just while explains mutch, can't explaine everything. You need Einsteinian laws, but they again, sotps working at a point (around the point the universe false to be static) and you need Hawking's laws, but again while Newton, Einstein and Hawking are working perfectly and bases of several things... they can't explain the Why completely just the How </div> </div> </div>False Equivalences are fun.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Werewolf, Material, Umbra all of them is the the <i>How</i><br /> The Elohim and their work is the <i>Why</i><br /> And the two are not contradicts or makes the other untrue!<br /> Creation, spirits, umbra, etc are just the stage, everything on it: the actors, the decorations, literally everything! The river and the spirit of the river, the material planes and spiritual worlds with tagging along paralel or overlaping universes and Qlippothic ones<br /> The Elohim and their work is the Why: the backstage, levers and pulleys and directors, run crew, stagehands, backstage crew, the professionals who work backstage during performances to keep the show running smoothly and safely and you ideally never could see and/or from the point of the audience, they not even exist<br /> And just like in Demon, the abscence of the backstage and the crew not necessarily means the Show on the stage can't go on (just without the supervision and support, eventually degrades)<br /> <br /> \u200b </div> </div> </div>I don't care. D:tF was a needless cash-in on In Nomine. It only ever touched on the Dark Umbra, and it seemed to steer away from Werewolf on fear that it would evaporate if it came into contact with it. Every part of it is, like Vampire, an optional antagonist that I can drop into an Apocalypse scenario, but probably won't, because W:tA has more than enough to go around, and with sea level rise becoming an issue as noted up thread, Chulorviah make a much more sensible set of antagonists for the future, in an Apocalypse scenario or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-14T20:23:03-08:00","id":1528577,"title":"","content":"In Nomine (the English version) came out in 1997 and was effectively a dead line by 2000. Demon the Fallen didn't come out til 2002. A bit late for a &quot;cash in&quot;, I suspect. Demon's real purpose was just to move the End Times/Final Nights closer. And a number of people at the time theorized the idea that the Malhim created after the Fall might be the &quot;secret origin&quot; of the Garou. Which it could be, if you wanted. Or not, if you don't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1},{"type":"\ud83e\udd22","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-14T23:36:48-08:00","id":1528581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1527695-suggested-setting-changes-to-make-crossover-easier?p=1528546#post1528546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23\" data-vbnamecard=\"23\">Saur Ops Specialist</a> isn't throwing Demon under the bus because they <b>have</b> to. They are doing it because they <b>want</b> to. And it makes sense from their POV.</div> </div> </div> </div>Naturally<br /> Have to and want to is two different thing <br /> And indeed, make sense from a certain point of view<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-15T03:03:31-08:00","id":1528582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1527695-suggested-setting-changes-to-make-crossover-easier?p=1528577#post1528577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In Nomine (the English version) came out in 1997 and was effectively a dead line by 2000. Demon the Fallen didn't come out til 2002. A bit late for a &quot;cash in&quot;, I suspect. Demon's real purpose was just to move the End Times/Final Nights closer. And a number of people at the time theorized the idea that the Malhim created after the Fall might be the &quot;secret origin&quot; of the Garou. Which it could be, if you wanted. Or not, if you don't.</div> </div> </div> </div>In Nomine was a much better demon game than DtF was, though. Better thought out, with multiple ways to interpret it and with an amazing setting that worked on its own, without needing to meddle with a dozen other lines. Mid to late Ninties had a number of games along those lines, and from what I remember of the conversations, Demon was not there because they were ending the lines, it was there because they wanted to make it, but by the time the first books were out the decision came to end it and restart everything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-15T04:22:14-08:00","id":1528584,"title":"","content":"In Nomine also was an adaptation of a French game, giving it a very strong foundation; also calling it &quot;dead&quot; after a short run of English books is kinda insulting to it's nearly 27 year publication history in French (1989 - 2016).<br /> <br /> DtF was sort of the in the middle. It wasn't made specifically to usher in the End Times, but it was intended to tie in heavily to the metaplot changes in Revised.<br /> <br /> Though I've also lost complete track of what the whole point of this debate even is anymore, despite reading all the posts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-15T10:46:54-08:00","id":1528605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1527695-suggested-setting-changes-to-make-crossover-easier?p=1528582#post1528582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Demon was not there because they were ending the lines, it was there because they wanted to make it, but by the time the first books were out the decision came to end it and restart everything.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not referring to Time of Judgement. I am referring to the entire Revised era's focus on it now being the end of days, starting with Vampire Revised being announced on the release schedule not by its title but as &quot;The Final Nights&quot; and everything that followed after (Week of Nightmares, Hunter the Reckoning, End of Empire, the return of the Silver Crown, Changeling's civil war, etc.). <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-15T10:58:39-08:00","id":1528607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1527695-suggested-setting-changes-to-make-crossover-easier?p=1528584#post1528584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In Nomine also was an adaptation of a French game, giving it a very strong foundation; also calling it &quot;dead&quot; after a short run of English books is kinda insulting to it's nearly 27 year publication history in French (1989 - 2016).<br /> <br /> DtF was sort of the in the middle. It wasn't made specifically to usher in the End Times, but it was intended to tie in heavily to the metaplot changes in Revised.<br /> <br /> Though I've also lost complete track of what the whole point of this debate even is anymore, despite reading all the posts.</div> </div> </div> </div>At this point, it's a question of which debate, haha. It started as a discussion about the challenges of integrating Vampires into Crossover in a friendly fashion. At some point it switched to <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23\" data-vbnamecard=\"23\">Saur Ops Specialist</a> and I going back and forth on the conflicts between Mage and Werewolf metaphysics, and the extent to which it's possible to harmonize the conflicts between them. And then <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23890_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23890\" data-vbnamecard=\"23890\">Shadeprowler</a> brought Demon into the discussion. I may have missed a stage or two in there.<br /> <br /> The In Nomine one kind of just popped up all of a sudden due to a comment that seems to have been made in passing; I don't know anything about In Nomine, so nothing really to add there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-15T11:04:09-08:00","id":1528608,"title":"","content":"Deleted .....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":12890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","user":"No One of Consequence","date":". 01-15-2024, 02:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-15T14:01:50-08:00","id":1528621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1527695-suggested-setting-changes-to-make-crossover-easier?p=1528605#post1528605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not referring to Time of Judgement. I am referring to the entire Revised era's focus on it now being the end of days, starting with Vampire Revised being announced on the release schedule not by its title but as &quot;The Final Nights&quot; and everything that followed after (Week of Nightmares, Hunter the Reckoning, End of Empire, the return of the Silver Crown, Changeling's civil war, etc.).</div> </div> </div> </div>Thing is, how &quot;Final&quot; the nights were really depended on the game to game. Mage started out very rough, but Revised in general was about rebuilding in creating new things and bringing back the old. It was quite good at that, and it wasn't really going towards a &quot;End of Days&quot;. It was horribly dissapointing to see that the book about Ascension was mostly Doomsday scenarios without actually engaging with the core ideas of Mage.<br /> <br /> Werewolf was going there, but it was also the edition of hope, activity and change where the nation was off its butt and the battle felt like you could get something out of it.<br /> <br /> Hunter did have a very apocalyptic vibe to it, but the further it got from the first book, the more it was building itself to be workable as an ongoing game without needing to commit to the End of Days, zombie apocalypse vibe it started out with.<br /> <br /> It was Vampire's fixation with Final Nights that was the problem there and it wasn't really relevant to the other games before the ToJ landed on them with a resounding thump. Most of the other games said &quot;Oh another Vampire huge upheaval happened somewhere, anyway back to our stuff...&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-15T15:52:06-08:00","id":1528626,"title":"","content":"Demon very much does not want to cooperate in crossover. It's kind of a problem child. Tack on how it's also very much playing to the crowd in its religious horror themes, and you have something that I'll throw under the bus over and over again, because it's just not worth accommodating it. There were already more than a few beings that were identified as &quot;demons&quot; in some way, so having Noddism 2.0: Take the Bible Even More Literally roll in was not inspiring in the least. It just seem to whip everyone already trying to wrap everything up in a very particular read of Christianity into a furor and give them the assurance that they were right (even though that Layers of Reality canard couldn't even explain more than Mage's take on things, and Mage can't even explain Mage to everyone's preferred extent).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1527695-suggested-setting-changes-to-make-crossover-easier?p=1528621#post1528621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thing is, how &quot;Final&quot; the nights were really depended on the game to game. Mage started out very rough, but Revised in general was about rebuilding in creating new things and bringing back the old. It was quite good at that, and it wasn't really going towards a &quot;End of Days&quot;. It was horribly dissapointing to see that the book about Ascension was mostly Doomsday scenarios without actually engaging with the core ideas of Mage.<br /> <br /> Werewolf was going there, but it was also the edition of hope, activity and change where the nation was off its butt and the battle felt like you could get something out of it.<br /> <br /> Hunter did have a very apocalyptic vibe to it, but the further it got from the first book, the more it was building itself to be workable as an ongoing game without needing to commit to the End of Days, zombie apocalypse vibe it started out with.</div> </div> </div> </div>A hidden zombie apocalypse at that, driven entirely by unquiet dead leftover from what people would likely have thought was the end of things, even though no one seemed to notice. You know what they say - the end is the beginning...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It was Vampire's fixation with Final Nights that was the problem there and it wasn't really relevant to the other games before the ToJ landed on them with a resounding thump. Most of the other games said &quot;Oh another Vampire huge upheaval happened somewhere, anyway back to our stuff...&quot; </div> </div> </div>Trumpet of Meru FTW! The Kindred won't even know what hit them when the Shih come onto the scene with 50-100 points of Chi to spend!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}